{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LBDC551Vjd8RgVRGMWeWU3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '放弃 ''general cross-representation diagnosis framework'' 的普适性叙事。Reframe\n2\t  为 domain-specific 深度研究：''When and Why Cross-Representation Disagreement Works: A\n3\t  Case Study in Formal Logic Reasoning''。核心 angle 转向：(1) 深度刻画 FOL-Code 分歧在逻辑推理中的独特有效性及其认知/结构原因，\n4\t  (2) 系统性分析跨域失败的原因（correlated failures、specification-level errors 的普遍性）， (3) 提出 cross-representation\n5\t  diagnosis 的 applicability conditions。用深度补广度，FOLIO 上 的分析必须足够深。\n6\t\n7\t  '\n8\timagined_experiments:\n9\t- name: Cross-Model Ablation (FOLIO)\n10\t  plan_id: exp-002\n11\t  description: DeepSeek V4 Pro 生成一种表征 + Qwen3-32B 生成另一种，测试模型多样性是否降低 correlated failures\n12\t  expected_results:\n13\t    C1_disagree_rate_mixed: 0.42\n14\t    C1_disagree_rate_deepseek_only: 0.33\n15\t    C2_diagnostic_precision_mixed: 0.83\n16\t    C2_diagnostic_precision_deepseek_only: 0.78\n17\t    false_agreement_reduction_vs_single_model_pp: 1.5\n18\t    correlated_failure_rate_single_model: 0.18\n19\t    correlated_failure_rate_mixed_model: 0.165\n20\t    C5_localization_mixed: 0.81\n21\t    new_disagreement_type_introduced: true\n22\t    spurious_disagreement_rate_mixed: 0.09\n23\t  result_rationale: '混合模型配置仅将 false agreement 降低约 1.5pp（从 ~18% 到 ~16.5%），远低于预期的 5-8pp。\n24\t    原因：correlated failures 的根源不在于 \"同一个模型的 shared bias\"，而在于 specification-level ambiguity——两个不同模型面对同一道模糊\n25\t    NL 问题时，犯相同的 specification error 的概率仍然很高， 因为错误来源是 NL 本身的歧义而非模型内部表征。DeepSeek V4\n26\t    Pro 单独运行时 disagree rate 更低（33% vs 39.6%），说明更强模型的两种表征更趋一致（能力提升同时减少了 formalization-specific\n27\t    errors 和 diagnostic opportunities）。混合模型引入约 9% 的 spurious disagreements——两个模型对\n28\t    同一问题的合法但不同的形式化选择（如变量命名、逻辑等价变换），这些分歧不是 errors 而是 representation divergence，降低了整体\n29\t    precision。结论：模型多样性不是解决 correlated failures 的有效路径， 因为 correlation 的主要来源是 task specification\n30\t    而非 model bias。\n31\t\n32\t    '\n33\t  tables:\n34\t  - table_id: tab-exp002-1\n35\t    caption: Cross-Model vs Single-Model Pipeline Comparison (FOLIO, N=192)\n36\t    columns:\n37\t    - Config\n38\t    - C1 Disagree%\n39\t    - C2 Precision%\n40\t    - Correlated Failure%\n41\t    - Spurious Disagree%\n42\t    - C5 Localization%\n43\t    rows:\n44\t    - - Qwen3-32B (single)\n45\t      - 39.6%\n46\t      - 86.8%\n47\t      - 18.2%\n48\t      - 3.1%\n49\t      - 85.4%\n50\t    - - DeepSeek V4 Pro (single)\n51\t      - 33.3%\n52\t      - 78.1%\n53\t      - 19.8%\n54\t      - 4.2%\n55\t      - 79.7%\n56\t    - - Mixed (DS-FOL, Qwen-Code)\n57\t      - 42.2%\n58\t      - 83.3%\n59\t      - 16.5%\n60\t      - 9.1%\n61\t      - 81.3%\n62\t    - - Mixed (Qwen-FOL, DS-Code)\n63\t      - 40.6%\n64\t      - 80.6%\n65\t      - 17.1%\n66\t      - 8.7%\n67\t      - 78.9%\n68\t  - table_id: tab-exp002-2\n69\t    caption: False Agreement Breakdown by Error Source\n70\t    columns:\n71\t    - Error Source\n72\t    - Single-Model False Agree%\n73\t    - Mixed-Model False Agree%\n74\t    - Δ\n75\t    rows:\n76\t    - - Specification-level ambiguity\n77\t      - 11.5%\n78\t      - 10.9%\n79\t      - -0.6pp\n80\t    - - Shared formalization bias\n81\t      - 4.2%\n82\t      - 3.1%\n83\t      - -1.1pp\n84\t    - - Independent coincidental\n85\t      - 2.5%\n86\t      - 2.5%\n87\t      - 0.0pp\n88\t  figures_description:\n89\t  - 'Venn diagram: Qwen-only failures vs DeepSeek-only failures vs shared failures,\n90\t    showing ~70% overlap in false-agreement samples across models — evidence that\n91\t    correlated failures are task-driven not model-driven'\n92\t  - 'Bar chart: spurious disagreement rate by disagreement category (legitimate formalization\n93\t    choice vs actual error), showing mixed-model introduces ~3x more spurious disagreements'\n94\t  analysis: '核心发现是 correlated failures 的主要来源是 task specification 而非 model bias，因此\n95\t    cross-model 策略的边际收益极小。这对 general framework 叙事是重大打击——如果 false agreement 无法通过模型多样性有效缓解，那么\n96\t    diagnosis coverage 存在固有上限。但这一 negative result 本身 具有 insight 价值：它揭示了 cross-representation\n97\t    diagnosis 的 fundamental limitation 来自 NL-to-formal 的 specification gap，而非模型能力。在\n98\t    reframed narrative 中，这成为 boundary characterization 的关键 evidence。\n99\t\n100\t    '\n101\t- name: ProofWriter Extension\n102\t  plan_id: exp-003\n103\t  description: 在 ProofWriter 上运行完整 pipeline，验证逻辑推理域内泛化性\n104\t  expected_results:\n105\t    N_samples: 300\n106\t    C1_disagree_rate: 0.17\n107\t    C2_diagnostic_precision: 0.63\n108\t    C3_error_types: 2\n109\t    C4_targeted_vs_blind_delta_pp_all_mode: 1.8\n110\t    C4_targeted_vs_blind_delta_pp_excl_unknown: -2.1\n111\t    C5_localization_accuracy: 0.72\n112\t    fol_code_error_ratio: '7:1'\n113\t    mvp_pass_count: 2/5 (C1 borderline FAIL at <20% threshold pending, C2 FAIL, C3\n114\t      PASS, C4 FAIL, C5 PASS)\n115\t    bootstrap_C1_95CI:\n116\t    - 0.13\n117\t    - 0.22\n118\t    bootstrap_C2_95CI:\n119\t    - 0.54\n120\t    - 0.71\n121\t    fisher_exact_C4_p_value: 0.31\n122\t  result_rationale: 'ProofWriter 的 disagree rate 仅 17%，远低于 FOLIO 的 39.6%。根本原因：ProofWriter\n123\t    的问题 结构高度规范化——前提以 \"If X then Y\" 的固定模板给出，推理深度可控（depth 0-5），NL 歧义极少。 这意味着 LLM 在 FOL\n124\t    和 Code 两种表征上都能较准确地捕获 specification，formalization-specific errors 的发生率本身就低。剩余的\n125\t    17% 分歧中，diagnostic precision 降至 63%：更多分歧来自 \"两种表征对 closed-world assumption 的不同处理\"——FOL/Z3\n126\t    默认 CWA 而 Python 代码常遗漏 CWA 导致的推理差异，这类分歧是 representation semantics gap 而非 formalization\n127\t    error。 error types 仅 2 种（缺少 FOLIO 上的 \"scope ambiguity\" 类型，因为 ProofWriter 无量词 作用域歧义）。Repair\n128\t    delta 仅 1.8pp（All-mode），因为可诊断的 errors 本身就少，且 CWA-related 分歧不可通过 repair 单侧修复。Excl-Unknown\n129\t    为负（-2.1pp），因为 ProofWriter 无 Unknown 类别，所有样本都是 True/False，移除了 FOLIO 上驱动 repair\n130\t    delta 的主要子集。\n131\t\n132\t    '\n133\t  tables:\n134\t  - table_id: tab-exp003-1\n135\t    caption: ProofWriter Full Pipeline Results (N=300, Qwen3-32B)\n136\t    columns:\n137\t    - Metric\n138\t    - ProofWriter\n139\t    - FOLIO (reference)\n140\t    - Δ\n141\t    rows:\n142\t    - - C1 Disagree Rate\n143\t      - 17.0% (42/247)\n144\t      - 39.6% (76/192)\n145\t      - -22.6pp\n146\t    - - C2 Diagnostic Precision\n147\t      - 63.2% (24/38)\n148\t      - 86.8% (66/76)\n149\t      - -23.6pp\n150\t    - - C3 Error Types\n151\t      - '2'\n152\t      - '3'\n153\t      - '-1'\n154\t    - - C4 Δ (All-mode)\n155\t      - +1.8pp\n156\t      - +5.2pp\n157\t      - -3.4pp\n158\t    - - C4 Δ (Excl-Unknown)\n159\t      - -2.1pp\n160\t      - +0.0pp\n161\t      - -2.1pp\n162\t    - - C5 Localization\n163\t      - 72.0%\n164\t      - 85.4%\n165\t      - -13.4pp\n166\t  - table_id: tab-exp003-2\n167\t    caption: 'Disagreement Source Analysis: ProofWriter vs FOLIO'\n168\t    columns:\n169\t    - Disagreement Source\n170\t    - ProofWriter %\n171\t    - FOLIO %\n172\t    rows:\n173\t    - - Formalization-specific error (one side wrong)\n174\t      - 63.2%\n175\t      - 86.8%\n176\t    - - CWA/semantic gap (neither side truly wrong)\n177\t      - 26.3%\n178\t      - 5.3%\n179\t    - - Both sides wrong (correlated failure)\n180\t      - 10.5%\n181\t      - 7.9%\n182\t  - table_id: tab-exp003-3\n183\t    caption: ProofWriter Results by Reasoning Depth\n184\t    columns:\n185\t    - Depth\n186\t    - N\n187\t    - Disagree%\n188\t    - Precision%\n189\t    - Notes\n190\t    rows:\n191\t    - - '0'\n192\t      - '62'\n193\t      - 8.1%\n194\t      - 40.0%\n195\t      - Trivial problems, few errors to detect\n196\t    - - '1'\n197\t      - '68'\n198\t      - 13.2%\n199\t      - 55.6%\n200\t      - Simple chain, low formalization difficulty\n201\t    - - '2'\n202\t      - '58'\n203\t      - 17.2%\n204\t      - 66.7%\n205\t      - Moderate depth\n206\t    - - '3'\n207\t      - '52'\n208\t      - 23.1%\n209\t      - 70.0%\n210\t      - More complex chains increase error rate\n211\t    - - '5'\n212\t      - '60'\n213\t      - 26.7%\n214\t      - 75.0%\n215\t      - Deepest reasoning shows highest signal\n216\t  figures_description:\n217\t  - 'Line plot: disagree rate and diagnostic precision vs reasoning depth (0-5), showing\n218\t    monotonic increase — signal improves with task complexity but even depth-5 falls\n219\t    below FOLIO baseline'\n220\t  - 'Confusion matrix: FOL vs Code correctness on ProofWriter, showing the 7:1 asymmetry\n221\t    persists but both sides are more accurate overall (fewer errors = fewer disagreements)'\n222\t  analysis: 'ProofWriter 结果确认了 worst-case 假设：诊断信号在结构化程度更高的 benchmark 上显著退化。 disagree\n223\t    rate 仅 17% 且 precision 仅 63%，均低于 FOLIO。关键 insight：cross-representation disagreement\n224\t    的 informativeness 与 NL specification 的 ambiguity 正相关——ProofWriter 的 \"clean\" NL\n225\t    减少了 formalization errors，但也减少了 diagnostic opportunities。 这不是方法的失败，而是 applicability\n226\t    boundary：当 NL→formal 翻译足够 straightforward 时，cross-representation diagnosis 的附加价值有限。depth-5\n227\t    子集数据（26.7% disagree, 75% precision）暗示在更难的推理链上信号恢复，为 \"complexity threshold\" 的 boundary\n228\t    condition 提供了 evidence。Reframed narrative 中，ProofWriter 作为 \"lower boundary\" 与\n229\t    FOLIO 的 \"sweet spot\" 形成对照。\n230\t\n231\t    '\n232\t- name: MATH Level 5 Extension\n233\t  plan_id: exp-004\n234\t  description: 在 MATH 难题子集运行 CoT vs SymPy/Python 双表征 pipeline\n235\t  expected_results:\n236\t    N_samples: 200\n237\t    C1_disagree_rate: 0.14\n238\t    C2_diagnostic_precision: 0.58\n239\t    C3_error_types: 3\n240\t    C4_targeted_vs_blind_delta_pp_all_mode: -0.5\n241\t    C4_targeted_vs_blind_delta_pp_excl_unknown: -3.2\n242\t    C5_localization_accuracy: 0.63\n243\t    cot_sympy_error_ratio: 1.8:1\n244\t    fol_code_error_ratio_equivalent: 7.2\n245\t    mvp_pass_count: 0/5 (all FAIL)\n246\t    bootstrap_C1_95CI:\n247\t    - 0.09\n248\t    - 0.19\n249\t    bootstrap_C2_95CI:\n250\t    - 0.47\n251\t    - 0.68\n252\t    fisher_exact_C4_p_value: 0.82\n253\t    correlated_failure_rate: 0.31\n254\t    specification_error_rate: 0.24\n255\t  result_rationale: 'MATH 域的双表征分歧模式与逻辑域本质不同，不支持统一框架叙事。核心原因有三： (1) 错误对称性逆转——CoT:SymPy\n256\t    error ratio 仅 1.8:1，远低于 FOLIO 的 9:1。数学推理中 CoT 的自然语言链式推导和 SymPy 的符号计算犯错概率更接近，因为数学\n257\t    errors 更多是 \"计算错误\" 而非 \"形式化翻译错误\"。FOL 在逻辑域近乎 \"ground truth\" 的角色（因为 Z3 solver 的完备性）\n258\t    在数学域不成立——SymPy 无法解决所有数学问题类型（如几何、组合），常 fallback 到数值近似。 (2) Correlated failure rate\n259\t    高达 31%——MATH Level 5 的难度意味着模型在 CoT 和 SymPy 两条路径上都无法正确 specify 问题（如组合恒等式、复杂积分），产生大量\n260\t    false agreement（双方 都错但碰巧同一答案或都无法执行）。 (3) 分歧的 diagnostic content 不同——MATH 上的分歧更多反映\n261\t    \"能否用该表征解决此类问题\" （capability mismatch）而非 \"形式化翻译是否正确\"（formalization quality）。例如 SymPy\n262\t    无法处理某些几何题，不是 formalization error 而是 tool limitation。 这导致 C2 precision 仅 58%，C5\n263\t    localization 仅 63%（因为 \"错误侧\" 的判定不明确—— 可能两侧都有道理但方法不同），repair delta 为负（targeted repair\n264\t    反而引入 noise）。\n265\t\n266\t    '\n267\t  tables:\n268\t  - table_id: tab-exp004-1\n269\t    caption: MATH Level 5 Full Pipeline Results (N=200, Qwen3-32B)\n270\t    columns:\n271\t    - Metric\n272\t    - MATH\n273\t    - FOLIO (ref)\n274\t    - ProofWriter (ref)\n275\t    rows:\n276\t    - - C1 Disagree Rate\n277\t      - 14.0% (24/172)\n278\t      - 39.6%\n279\t      - 17.0%\n280\t    - - C2 Diagnostic Precision\n281\t      - 58.3% (14/24)\n282\t      - 86.8%\n283\t      - 63.2%\n284\t    - - C3 Error Types\n285\t      - '3'\n286\t      - '3'\n287\t      - '2'\n288\t    - - C4 Δ All-mode\n289\t      - -0.5pp\n290\t      - +5.2pp\n291\t      - +1.8pp\n292\t    - - C4 Δ Excl-Unk\n293\t      - -3.2pp\n294\t      - +0.0pp\n295\t      - -2.1pp\n296\t    - - C5 Localization\n297\t      - 63.0%\n298\t      - 85.4%\n299\t      - 72.0%\n300\t    - - Error Ratio (logic:code equiv)\n301\t      - 1.8:1\n302\t      - '9:1'\n303\t      - '7:1'\n304\t    - - Correlated Failure Rate\n305\t      - 31.0%\n306\t      - 18.2%\n307\t      - 10.5%\n308\t  - table_id: tab-exp004-2\n309\t    caption: MATH Disagreement Source by Problem Category\n310\t    columns:\n311\t    - MATH Category\n312\t    - N\n313\t    - Disagree%\n314\t    - Precision%\n315\t    - CoT:SymPy Error Ratio\n316\t    rows:\n317\t    - - Algebra\n318\t      - '52'\n319\t      - 17.3%\n320\t      - 71.4%\n321\t      - 2.5:1\n322\t    - - Number Theory\n323\t      - '38'\n324\t      - 15.8%\n325\t      - 60.0%\n326\t      - 2.0:1\n327\t    - - Counting & Prob\n328\t      - '35'\n329\t      - 11.4%\n330\t      - 50.0%\n331\t      - 1.5:1\n332\t    - - Geometry\n333\t      - '28'\n334\t      - 10.7%\n335\t      - 33.3%\n336\t      - 1.0:1\n337\t    - - Precalculus\n338\t      - '25'\n339\t      - 12.0%\n340\t      - 50.0%\n341\t      - 1.2:1\n342\t    - - Intermediate Algebra\n343\t      - '22'\n344\t      - 18.2%\n345\t      - 66.7%\n346\t      - 2.2:1\n347\t  - table_id: tab-exp004-3\n348\t    caption: 'Error Type Distribution: MATH vs Logic Domains'\n349\t    columns:\n350\t    - Error Type\n351\t    - MATH %\n352\t    - FOLIO %\n353\t    - Interpretation\n354\t    rows:\n355\t    - - Formalization-specific\n356\t      - 33%\n357\t      - 72%\n358\t      - Much less dominant in MATH\n359\t    - - Specification-level\n360\t      - 24%\n361\t      - 10%\n362\t      - NL→formal ambiguity higher in MATH\n363\t    - - Tool limitation\n364\t      - 28%\n365\t      - 0%\n366\t      - SymPy can't solve certain problem types\n367\t    - - Computational error\n368\t      - 15%\n369\t      - 18%\n370\t      - Similar across domains\n371\t  figures_description:\n372\t  - 'Scatter plot: CoT accuracy vs SymPy accuracy per MATH category, showing near-diagonal\n373\t    clustering (error ratio ~1.8:1) vs FOLIO''s extreme off-diagonal (9:1) — the asymmetry\n374\t    that makes diagnosis work in logic does not exist in math'\n375\t  - 'Stacked bar: error source distribution across three benchmarks (FOLIO/ProofWriter/MATH),\n376\t    showing formalization-specific errors declining from 72% to 33% while specification-level\n377\t    and tool-limitation errors grow'\n378\t  - 'Heatmap: false agreement rate by MATH difficulty sublevel and category, showing\n379\t    concentrated failure in geometry and combinatorics'\n380\t  analysis: 'MATH 结果是 worst-case 的核心 evidence。0/5 MVP pass 意味着 cross-representation\n381\t    diagnosis 在数学域基本失效。关键 insight：诊断方法的有效性依赖于两种表征之间的 \"asymmetric reliability\"——在逻辑域，Z3\n382\t    的完备性保证了 FOL 侧几乎总是对的，使分歧成为高质量的 error detector。数学域缺少这种 asymmetry：CoT 和 SymPy 都是\n383\t    \"fallible solvers\"，分歧不再指向 \"哪边错了\"而是 \"两种方法对此题的适用性不同\"。Tool limitation（28%）作为新 error\n384\t    type 出现，这类错误不可通过 repair 修复（SymPy 本身不支持的问题类型）。 在 reframed narrative 中，这构成了 \"applicability\n385\t    condition\" 的核心论据： cross-representation diagnosis requires asymmetric reliability\n386\t    between representations， 而这在 formal logic 域自然成立（Z3 completeness）但在其他域不保证。\n387\t\n388\t    '\n389\t- name: Repair Mechanism Improvement\n390\t  plan_id: exp-005\n391\t  description: 多轮 repair + 错误类型特定修复策略，尝试拉大 targeted vs blind 差距\n392\t  expected_results:\n393\t    C4_round1_delta_pp_all_mode: 5.2\n394\t    C4_round2_delta_pp_all_mode: 2.6\n395\t    C4_round3_delta_pp_all_mode: 2.1\n396\t    C4_improved_prompt_delta_pp_all_mode: 3.0\n397\t    C4_best_config_delta_pp_all_mode: 3.0\n398\t    C4_best_config_delta_pp_excl_unknown: -1.5\n399\t    repair_success_rate_formalization_errors: 0.22\n400\t    repair_success_rate_specification_errors: 0.04\n401\t    multi_round_diminishing_returns: true\n402\t    error_type_specific_vs_generic_delta: 0.8\n403\t  result_rationale: '多轮 repair 和改进 prompt 均未能突破 C4 delta 瓶颈。原因分析： (1) 多轮 repair 呈显著递减收益——Round\n404\t    1 的 5.2pp 到 Round 2 降至 2.6pp，Round 3 仅 2.1pp。这是因为 Round 1 已修复了 \"easy fixes\"（简单的语法级\n405\t    formalization errors）， 剩余的 errors 是 deep semantic misunderstandings（模型对 NL 含义的理解偏差），多轮\n406\t    regeneration 不改变模型的理解。 (2) 改进 prompt（加入 error type 信息）的 delta 反而降至 3.0pp——更详细的\n407\t    diagnosis 信息有时误导 repair：当 error type classification 本身有 ~15% 错误率时，提供错误的 error\n408\t    type 信息比不提供更差。 (3) Excl-Unknown 从 0.0pp 恶化到 -1.5pp——多轮 repair 在 True/False 样本上引入了\n409\t    regression（过度修改导致原本正确的逻辑被破坏）。 (4) 核心瓶颈：repair 只能修复 formalization-specific errors（22%\n410\t    成功率），对 specification-level errors 几乎无效（4%），而后者占 errors 的 ~30%。targeted repair\n411\t    的上限被 error type 分布锁定。\n412\t\n413\t    '\n414\t  tables:\n415\t  - table_id: tab-exp005-1\n416\t    caption: Multi-Round Repair Results (FOLIO, N=96 disagreement pairs)\n417\t    columns:\n418\t    - Config\n419\t    - Targeted Acc\n420\t    - Blind Acc\n421\t    - Δ (pp)\n422\t    - Excl-Unk Δ (pp)\n423\t    rows:\n424\t    - - Baseline (Round 1, original prompt)\n425\t      - 63.5%\n426\t      - 58.3%\n427\t      - '+5.2'\n428\t      - '+0.0'\n429\t    - - Round 2 (re-repair failures)\n430\t      - 64.6%\n431\t      - 62.0%\n432\t      - '+2.6'\n433\t      - '-0.5'\n434\t    - - Round 3 (re-repair failures)\n435\t      - 65.1%\n436\t      - 63.0%\n437\t      - '+2.1'\n438\t      - '-1.0'\n439\t    - - Improved prompt (error-type-specific)\n440\t      - 62.5%\n441\t      - 59.5%\n442\t      - '+3.0'\n443\t      - '-1.5'\n444\t    - - Best combo (Round 2 + improved)\n445\t      - 63.8%\n446\t      - 60.8%\n447\t      - '+3.0'\n448\t      - '-1.5'\n449\t  - table_id: tab-exp005-2\n450\t    caption: Repair Success Rate by Error Type\n451\t    columns:\n452\t    - Error Type\n453\t    - N (targeted)\n454\t    - Repair Success%\n455\t    - Blind Success%\n456\t    - Δ\n457\t    rows:\n458\t    - - Variable mapping error\n459\t      - '18'\n460\t      - 33.3%\n461\t      - 22.2%\n462\t      - +11.1pp\n463\t    - - Scope/quantifier error\n464\t      - '12'\n465\t      - 16.7%\n466\t      - 16.7%\n467\t      - +0.0pp\n468\t    - - Logic connective error\n469\t      - '15'\n470\t      - 26.7%\n471\t      - 20.0%\n472\t      - +6.7pp\n473\t    - - Specification-level error\n474\t      - '9'\n475\t      - 4.4%\n476\t      - 6.7%\n477\t      - -2.2pp\n478\t    - - Unknown GT (all errors)\n479\t      - '42'\n480\t      - 28.6%\n481\t      - 19.0%\n482\t      - +9.5pp\n483\t  figures_description:\n484\t  - 'Line plot: C4 delta (pp) across repair rounds (1-3), showing monotonic decrease\n485\t    — diminishing returns curve with inflection at Round 1'\n486\t  - 'Grouped bar chart: repair success rate by error type for targeted vs blind, showing\n487\t    targeted advantage concentrates on variable-mapping and logic-connective errors\n488\t    while specification errors show no benefit'\n489\t  analysis: 'Repair improvement 实验确认了 C4 delta 的 structural ceiling。最佳配置仅 3.0pp All-mode（低于\n490\t    MVP 的 5.2pp，因为 improved prompt 有时误导），Excl-Unknown 为负。 这是 worst-case 的关键：即使投入 3\n491\t    rounds repair + error-type-specific prompts， targeted repair 相比 blind 的优势依然 marginal。根本原因是\n492\t    diagnosis 信息对 repair 的 actionability 有限——知道 \"Code 侧有 variable mapping error\" 并不能帮助\n493\t    LLM 在 重新生成时避免同样的错误，因为错误来源于 LLM 对 NL 语义的理解而非生成随机性。 在 reframed narrative 中，这支持 \"diagnosis\n494\t    as analysis tool, not repair tool\" 的定位。\n495\t\n496\t    '\n497\t- name: Unknown Sample Deep Analysis\n498\t  plan_id: exp-006\n499\t  description: 分析 GT=Unknown 样本为何驱动 C4 delta，探索 specification-level vs formalization-specific\n500\t    差异\n501\t  expected_results:\n502\t    unknown_sample_count: 66\n503\t    unknown_disagree_rate: 0.47\n504\t    unknown_specification_error_rate: 0.08\n505\t    unknown_formalization_error_rate: 0.39\n506\t    true_false_specification_error_rate: 0.22\n507\t    true_false_formalization_error_rate: 0.14\n508\t    unknown_fol_code_error_ratio: '12:1'\n509\t    true_false_fol_code_error_ratio: '6:1'\n510\t    unknown_repair_delta_pp: 9.5\n511\t    true_false_repair_delta_pp: -1.7\n512\t  result_rationale: 'Unknown 样本驱动 C4 delta 的原因在 worst-case 下被揭示为一个 confound 而非 feature：\n513\t    (1) Unknown 样本的 FOL:Code asymmetry 更极端（12:1 vs 6:1）——Z3 solver 对 \"信息不足\" 的判定（返回\n514\t    Unknown）几乎总是正确的，而 Python 代码极难正确实现 \"三值逻辑\"（True/False/Unknown）， 倾向于错误地返回 True 或\n515\t    False。这不是 \"diagnosis 发现了 formalization error\" 而是 \"Code 表征在结构上不适合处理 Unknown 类别\"。\n516\t    (2) True/False 样本的 specification error rate 更高（22% vs 8%），因为需要完整的 逻辑推理链，任何 NL\n517\t    歧义都传播为 specification error。Unknown 样本通常只需检测 \"信息不足\"， specification 更简单。 (3) 这意味着\n518\t    FOLIO 上的 C4 success 本质上是 \"Z3 对 Unknown 判定的优越性\" 的 side effect， 而非 cross-representation\n519\t    diagnosis 的 general 能力。当移除 Unknown 样本后 C4 delta 消失 就是这个 confound 的直接证据。\n520\t\n521\t    '\n522\t  tables:\n523\t  - table_id: tab-exp006-1\n524\t    caption: 'Error Mode Distribution: Unknown vs True/False Samples'\n525\t    columns:\n526\t    - Metric\n527\t    - GT=Unknown (N=66)\n528\t    - GT=True/False (N=126)\n529\t    - Interpretation\n530\t    rows:\n531\t    - - Disagree Rate\n532\t      - 47.0%\n533\t      - 35.7%\n534\t      - Unknown samples produce more disagreement\n535\t    - - Specification Error Rate\n536\t      - 8.1%\n537\t      - 22.2%\n538\t      - True/False problems have more NL ambiguity\n539\t    - - Formalization Error Rate\n540\t      - 39.4%\n541\t      - 14.3%\n542\t      - Unknown triggers Code-side errors\n543\t    - - FOL:Code Error Ratio\n544\t      - '12:1'\n545\t      - '6:1'\n546\t      - Extreme asymmetry on Unknown\n547\t    - - Code 'Unknown' output rate\n548\t      - 12.1%\n549\t      - N/A\n550\t      - Code rarely outputs Unknown correctly\n551\t    - - Repair Δ (targeted vs blind)\n552\t      - +9.5pp\n553\t      - -1.7pp\n554\t      - Entire C4 signal from Unknown\n555\t  - table_id: tab-exp006-2\n556\t    caption: Code-side Error Patterns on Unknown Samples\n557\t    columns:\n558\t    - Code Output\n559\t    - Count\n560\t    - '%'\n561\t    - Is Error?\n562\t    rows:\n563\t    - - True (should be Unknown)\n564\t      - '18'\n565\t      - 58.1%\n566\t      - Yes — most common failure\n567\t    - - False (should be Unknown)\n568\t      - '9'\n569\t      - 29.0%\n570\t      - 'Yes'\n571\t    - - Unknown (correct)\n572\t      - '3'\n573\t      - 9.7%\n574\t      - 'No'\n575\t    - - Runtime Error\n576\t      - '1'\n577\t      - 3.2%\n578\t      - 'Yes'\n579\t  figures_description:\n580\t  - 'Stacked bar: error type distribution split by GT label (Unknown / True / False),\n581\t    showing formalization errors dominate Unknown while specification errors dominate\n582\t    True/False'\n583\t  - 'Decision tree visualization: why Unknown samples are ''easy'' for diagnosis —\n584\t    Z3 returns Unknown → almost certainly correct → any Code disagreement is Code-side\n585\t    error → repair = regenerate Code'\n586\t  analysis: '这个分析在 worst-case scenario 中具有双刃剑效应。一方面，它解释了 C4 delta 的来源并揭示了 一个重要的 confound：FOLIO\n587\t    上的 repair success 主要来自 Unknown 样本中 Code 表征对三值逻辑 的结构性缺陷，而非 diagnosis 的 general\n588\t    能力。另一方面，在 reframed narrative 中，这恰好 是 \"When and Why\" 的深度案例：精确刻画了 WHY diagnosis\n589\t    works（Z3 completeness + representation asymmetry）和 WHEN it fails（True/False samples\n590\t    where specification errors dominate）。这个 confound 的发现本身是 contribution——它警告后续研究者\n591\t    cross-representation diagnosis 的效果可能被特定 GT label 分布所夸大。\n592\t\n593\t    '\n594\t- name: Selection vs Repair Ablation\n595\t  plan_id: exp-007\n596\t  description: 检测到分歧后，直接选择另一侧 vs 诊断引导修复的对比\n597\t  expected_results:\n598\t    selection_accuracy_all_mode: 0.68\n599\t    repair_accuracy_all_mode: 0.635\n600\t    selection_vs_repair_delta_pp: 4.5\n601\t    selection_accuracy_excl_unknown: 0.61\n602\t    repair_accuracy_excl_unknown: 0.59\n603\t    selection_accuracy_when_localization_correct: 0.8\n604\t    selection_accuracy_when_localization_wrong: 0.31\n605\t    oracle_selection_accuracy: 0.88\n606\t  result_rationale: 'Selection（直接选正确侧）在 All-mode 上以 4.5pp 优于 Repair（68% vs 63.5%），这对\n607\t    repair contribution 是直接打击。原因： (1) 在 9:1 的 FOL:Code asymmetry 下，\"永远选 FOL\" 这个 naive\n608\t    策略本身就有 ~90% 的 accuracy on disagreement samples。Selection with localization（选 localization\n609\t    判定的 正确侧）达到 68%（受限于 localization 的 85% accuracy——当 localization 错误时 selection 反而选了错误侧，降至\n610\t    31%）。 (2) Repair 的 63.5% 低于 selection 的 68%，因为 repair 引入了 regeneration noise——\n611\t    即使 diagnosis 正确指出了错误侧和错误类型，LLM 的重新生成不保证修复该错误，有时甚至引入新错误。 (3) Oracle selection（假设\n612\t    perfect localization）达到 88%，说明 localization accuracy 是 selection 策略的主要瓶颈。这暗示 \"提升\n613\t    localization\" 比 \"提升 repair\" 更有杠杆。 在 worst-case 下，这意味着 repair 作为 downstream application\n614\t    不仅 marginal 而且 不如更简单的 selection baseline。\n615\t\n616\t    '\n617\t  tables:\n618\t  - table_id: tab-exp007-1\n619\t    caption: Selection vs Repair Comparison (FOLIO disagreement samples)\n620\t    columns:\n621\t    - Strategy\n622\t    - All-mode Acc\n623\t    - Excl-Unk Acc\n624\t    - Compute Cost (relative)\n625\t    rows:\n626\t    - - Always-FOL baseline\n627\t      - 65.8%\n628\t      - 57.8%\n629\t      - 0x (no extra)\n630\t    - - Selection (w/ localization)\n631\t      - 68.0%\n632\t      - 61.0%\n633\t      - 0x (no extra)\n634\t    - - Repair (targeted, 1 round)\n635\t      - 63.5%\n636\t      - 59.3%\n637\t      - 1x (regeneration)\n638\t    - - Repair (targeted, 3 rounds)\n639\t      - 65.1%\n640\t      - 57.6%\n641\t      - 3x\n642\t    - - Oracle Selection\n643\t      - 88.0%\n644\t      - 82.0%\n645\t      - 0x (hypothetical)\n646\t    - - Blind Repair (1 round)\n647\t      - 58.3%\n648\t      - 59.3%\n649\t      - 1x\n650\t  - table_id: tab-exp007-2\n651\t    caption: Selection Accuracy Conditioned on Localization Correctness\n652\t    columns:\n653\t    - Localization\n654\t    - N\n655\t    - Selection Acc\n656\t    - Repair Acc\n657\t    rows:\n658\t    - - Correct (85.4%)\n659\t      - '35'\n660\t      - 80.0%\n661\t      - 68.6%\n662\t    - - Incorrect (14.6%)\n663\t      - '6'\n664\t      - 31.3%\n665\t      - 50.0%\n666\t  figures_description:\n667\t  - 'Bar chart with error bars: accuracy comparison across 5 strategies (always-FOL,\n668\t    selection, repair-1, repair-3, oracle-selection), showing selection > repair and\n669\t    oracle-selection sets the ceiling'\n670\t  - 'Scatter: per-sample selection outcome vs repair outcome, showing weak correlation\n671\t    (r=0.32) — selection and repair succeed on different subsets'\n672\t  analysis: 'Selection > Repair 的结果在 worst-case 中直接质疑了 repair 作为 downstream application\n673\t    的价值。一个更简单、零额外计算成本的策略（selection）beats 更复杂、需要额外 LLM call 的策略 （repair），这在 reviewer\n674\t    眼中是 fatal weakness for the repair narrative。然而在 reframed narrative 中，这反而支持 \"diagnosis\n675\t    as analysis, not repair\" 的定位：cross-representation disagreement 的价值在于 detection\n676\t    和 localization，不在于 repair。Selection 的成功 恰好证明 diagnosis 的上游价值（localization accuracy\n677\t    直接决定 selection quality）。 Oracle selection 88% 的上限暗示未来方向：提升 localization 精度是 highest-leverage\n678\t    improvement。\n679\t\n680\t    '\n681\t- name: Error Taxonomy Ablation\n682\t  plan_id: exp-008\n683\t  description: 按错误类型分派修复策略 vs 固定策略的对比\n684\t  expected_results:\n685\t    taxonomy_guided_repair_acc: 0.625\n686\t    fixed_strategy_repair_acc: 0.615\n687\t    taxonomy_vs_fixed_delta_pp: 1.0\n688\t    taxonomy_guided_by_error_type:\n689\t      variable_mapping: 0.333\n690\t      scope_quantifier: 0.167\n691\t      logic_connective: 0.267\n692\t    fixed_strategy_by_error_type:\n693\t      variable_mapping: 0.278\n694\t      scope_quantifier: 0.167\n695\t      logic_connective: 0.2\n696\t    taxonomy_misclassification_rate: 0.15\n697\t    taxonomy_misclassification_repair_success: 0.07\n698\t  result_rationale: 'Taxonomy-guided repair 仅比 fixed strategy 高 1.0pp（62.5% vs 61.5%），在\n699\t    worst-case 下这个差异统计不显著（p=0.68, Fisher exact test）。原因： (1) Error taxonomy 的分类准确率约\n700\t    85%，那 15% 的 misclassification 会导致错误的修复策略 被应用，反而降低 repair 效果——misclassified samples\n701\t    的 repair 成功率仅 7%（vs correctly classified 的 ~25%）。 (2) 不同 error type 的最优修复策略差异不大——无论是\n702\t    variable mapping error 还是 logic connective error，LLM 的 repair 本质上都是 \"重新生成并希望这次不犯同样的错\"。Error\n703\t    type 信息对 repair prompt 的 marginal guidance 有限，因为 LLM 不能精确执行 \"只修改变量映射 而保持其他逻辑不变\"\n704\t    这样的指令。 (3) Scope/quantifier errors 在两种策略下 repair 成功率相同（16.7%），说明这类 deep semantic\n705\t    errors 超出了 prompt-level repair 的能力边界。\n706\t\n707\t    '\n708\t  tables:\n709\t  - table_id: tab-exp008-1\n710\t    caption: Taxonomy-Guided vs Fixed Strategy Repair (FOLIO)\n711\t    columns:\n712\t    - Strategy\n713\t    - Overall Acc\n714\t    - Variable Map\n715\t    - Scope/Quant\n716\t    - Logic Conn\n717\t    - p-value\n718\t    rows:\n719\t    - - Taxonomy-guided\n720\t      - 62.5%\n721\t      - 33.3%\n722\t      - 16.7%\n723\t      - 26.7%\n724\t      - ''\n725\t    - - Fixed (generic regen)\n726\t      - 61.5%\n727\t      - 27.8%\n728\t      - 16.7%\n729\t      - 20.0%\n730\t      - '0.68'\n731\t    - - Δ\n732\t      - +1.0pp\n733\t      - +5.5pp\n734\t      - +0.0pp\n735\t      - +6.7pp\n736\t      - n.s.\n737\t  - table_id: tab-exp008-2\n738\t    caption: Impact of Taxonomy Misclassification on Repair\n739\t    columns:\n740\t    - Classification\n741\t    - N\n742\t    - Repair Success%\n743\t    - Notes\n744\t    rows:\n745\t    - - Correctly classified\n746\t      - '36'\n747\t      - 25.0%\n748\t      - Taxonomy info slightly helps\n749\t    - - Misclassified\n750\t      - '5'\n751\t      - 7.1%\n752\t      - Wrong repair strategy applied\n753\t    - - All targeted\n754\t      - '41'\n755\t      - 22.0%\n756\t      - Weighted average\n757\t  figures_description:\n758\t  - 'Grouped bar: repair success rate per error type, taxonomy-guided vs fixed, with\n759\t    95% CI error bars overlapping on all types'\n760\t  - 'Sankey diagram: error type classification → repair strategy → outcome, showing\n761\t    misclassification paths leading to failures'\n762\t  analysis: 'Taxonomy 的规定性价值在 worst-case 下几乎不存在。1.0pp 的差异在 N=41 的样本量下统计不显著， 无法 claim\n763\t    taxonomy-guided repair is better than generic repair。这对论文的 error taxonomy contribution\n764\t    有影响——如果 taxonomy 只有 descriptive value（帮助理解 errors） 而无 prescriptive value（指导 repair），reviewer\n765\t    可能质疑 taxonomy 的实用性。 在 reframed narrative 中，taxonomy 的价值重新定位为 analytical tool：它帮助解释\n766\t    WHY 某些 errors 可修复而某些不可修复（scope errors 的 0% Δ），贡献于 boundary characterization 而非\n767\t    repair improvement。\n768\t\n769\t    '\n770\t- name: Statistical Significance Testing\n771\t  plan_id: exp-009\n772\t  description: 对所有 benchmark 做 bootstrap 95% CI + Fisher exact test\n773\t  expected_results:\n774\t    folio_C1_bootstrap_95CI:\n775\t    - 0.333\n776\t    - 0.461\n777\t    folio_C2_bootstrap_95CI:\n778\t    - 0.782\n779\t    - 0.934\n780\t    folio_C4_bootstrap_95CI_all_mode:\n781\t    - -0.8\n782\t    - 11.2\n783\t    folio_C4_fisher_p_all_mode: 0.078\n784\t    folio_C4_bootstrap_95CI_excl_unknown:\n785\t    - -7.5\n786\t    - 7.5\n787\t    folio_C4_fisher_p_excl_unknown: 1.0\n788\t    folio_C5_bootstrap_95CI:\n789\t    - 0.735\n790\t    - 0.939\n791\t    proofwriter_C1_bootstrap_95CI:\n792\t    - 0.128\n793\t    - 0.218\n794\t    proofwriter_C2_bootstrap_95CI:\n795\t    - 0.472\n796\t    - 0.771\n797\t    proofwriter_C4_fisher_p: 0.31\n798\t    math_C1_bootstrap_95CI:\n799\t    - 0.093\n800\t    - 0.194\n801\t    math_C2_bootstrap_95CI:\n802\t    - 0.385\n803\t    - 0.762\n804\t    math_C4_fisher_p: 0.82\n805\t    benchmarks_with_C4_significant: 0\n806\t    benchmarks_with_C1C2_significant: 1\n807\t  result_rationale: '统计显著性结果在 worst-case 下呈现清晰的 \"FOLIO-only\" 格局： (1) FOLIO 的 C1（39.6%）和\n808\t    C2（86.8%）CI 不跨零，统计显著。但 C4 All-mode（+5.2pp） 的 Fisher exact p=0.078，未达 0.05 阈值——这是因为\n809\t    C4 的 base rate 比较（targeted vs blind） 在 N=96 paired samples 上 power 不足。Bootstrap\n810\t    CI [-0.8, 11.2] 跨零。Excl-Unknown 的 C4 delta=0.0pp 显然不显著。 (2) ProofWriter 的 C2 CI\n811\t    [0.472, 0.771] 跨 65% threshold——无法 claim \"high precision\"。 C4 p=0.31，far from\n812\t    significant。 (3) MATH 更差：C2 CI [0.385, 0.762] 极宽（N=24 disagreement samples），C4\n813\t    p=0.82。 (4) 没有任何 benchmark 的 C4 达到统计显著性。只有 FOLIO 的 C1 和 C2 显著。 这意味着论文能统计支撑的 claim\n814\t    仅限于 \"FOLIO 上 disagree rate substantial 且 diagnostically precise\"，repair 和跨域泛化均无统计支撑。\n815\t\n816\t    '\n817\t  tables:\n818\t  - table_id: tab-exp009-1\n819\t    caption: Statistical Significance Summary Across Benchmarks\n820\t    columns:\n821\t    - Metric\n822\t    - FOLIO\n823\t    - ProofWriter\n824\t    - MATH\n825\t    rows:\n826\t    - - C1 Disagree Rate\n827\t      - 39.6% [33.3, 46.1]**\n828\t      - 17.0% [12.8, 21.8]*\n829\t      - 14.0% [9.3, 19.4]*\n830\t    - - C2 Precision\n831\t      - 86.8% [78.2, 93.4]**\n832\t      - 63.2% [47.2, 77.1]\n833\t      - 58.3% [38.5, 76.2]\n834\t    - - C4 Δ All-mode\n835\t      - +5.2pp [-0.8, 11.2]\n836\t      - +1.8pp [-4.2, 7.8]\n837\t      - -0.5pp [-9.1, 8.1]\n838\t    - - C4 Fisher p (All)\n839\t      - '0.078'\n840\t      - '0.31'\n841\t      - '0.82'\n842\t    - - C4 Δ Excl-Unk\n843\t      - +0.0pp [-7.5, 7.5]\n844\t      - -2.1pp [-9.8, 5.6]\n845\t      - -3.2pp [-14.1, 7.7]\n846\t    - - C5 Localization\n847\t      - 85.4% [73.5, 93.9]**\n848\t      - 72.0% [58.1, 83.5]*\n849\t      - 63.0% [44.7, 79.0]\n850\t  - table_id: tab-exp009-2\n851\t    caption: Statistical Power Analysis\n852\t    columns:\n853\t    - Test\n854\t    - N (effective)\n855\t    - Observed Effect\n856\t    - Power at α=0.05\n857\t    - N needed for 80% power\n858\t    rows:\n859\t    - - FOLIO C4 Fisher\n860\t      - 96 pairs\n861\t      - +5.2pp\n862\t      - '0.42'\n863\t      - ~280\n864\t    - - ProofWriter C4 Fisher\n865\t      - ~120 pairs\n866\t      - +1.8pp\n867\t      - '0.12'\n868\t      - ~2400\n869\t    - - MATH C4 Fisher\n870\t      - ~86 pairs\n871\t      - -0.5pp\n872\t      - '0.05'\n873\t      - N/A (null effect)\n874\t  figures_description:\n875\t  - 'Forest plot: C4 delta with 95% CI across three benchmarks, showing all CIs crossing\n876\t    zero — no benchmark achieves statistical significance for repair'\n877\t  - 'Forest plot: C2 precision with 95% CI, showing FOLIO clearly above 65% threshold\n878\t    while ProofWriter and MATH CIs cross it'\n879\t  - 'Power curve: statistical power vs sample size for C4 Fisher test at observed\n880\t    effect sizes, showing FOLIO needs ~280 samples for 80% power'\n881\t  analysis: '统计检验结果是 worst-case 的 \"nail in the coffin\" for the general framework narrative。\n882\t    C4（repair）在任何 benchmark 上都不显著，C2（precision）仅在 FOLIO 上显著。 这直接支持核心假设 \"仅 FOLIO 单\n883\t    benchmark 数据可靠\"。 在 reframed narrative 中，这驱动两个调整：(1) 诚实报告 all CIs，不 overclaim；\n884\t    (2) 将 FOLIO 的 power analysis 作为 future work 的 guide（需要 ~280 samples 才能 confirm\n885\t    C4 effect），承认当前 sample size 是 limitation。 注意 FOLIO C4 的 p=0.078 是 borderline——在\n886\t    reframed 的 \"case study\" narrative 下， 可以 report 为 \"marginally significant trend\"\n887\t    而非 hard claim，这在 EMNLP 可接受。\n888\t\n889\t    '\n890\t- name: Qwen3-8B Ablation\n891\t  plan_id: exp-010\n892\t  description: 低能力模型上的诊断率和分歧率测试\n893\t  expected_results:\n894\t    C1_disagree_rate: 0.52\n895\t    C2_diagnostic_precision: 0.61\n896\t    C3_error_types: 3\n897\t    C4_targeted_vs_blind_delta_pp: 1.5\n898\t    C5_localization_accuracy: 0.68\n899\t    fol_code_error_ratio: '4:1'\n900\t    fol_crash_rate: 0.12\n901\t    code_crash_rate: 0.08\n902\t    both_wrong_rate: 0.28\n903\t  result_rationale: 'Qwen3-8B 的 disagree rate 上升到 52%（vs 32B 的 39.6%），表面上看更多分歧。但 diagnostic\n904\t    precision 降至 61%——更多分歧是 \"noise\" 而非 \"signal\"。原因： (1) 8B 模型在两种表征上都犯更多错误，both-wrong\n905\t    rate 从 ~10% 飙升到 28%。大量 disagreements 来自 \"两侧都错但错误方式不同\"，这类分歧无 diagnostic value。\n906\t    (2) FOL:Code asymmetry 减弱（4:1 vs 9:1）——8B 的 FOL 生成能力退化明显（Z3 crash rate 12%，因为生成的\n907\t    FOL 语法更常出错），削弱了 \"FOL 作为 reliable reference\" 的前提。 (3) C4 delta 仅 1.5pp——更多错误不等于更多可修复的错误。低能力模型的\n908\t    errors 更 fundamental （理解错误而非形式化错误），repair 更难。 (4) C5 localization 降至 68%——当 both-wrong\n909\t    rate 高时，\"哪侧错了\" 的判定本身就更模糊。\n910\t\n911\t    '\n912\t  tables:\n913\t  - table_id: tab-exp010-1\n914\t    caption: 'Model Capability Ablation: Qwen3-8B vs Qwen3-32B (FOLIO)'\n915\t    columns:\n916\t    - Metric\n917\t    - Qwen3-8B\n918\t    - Qwen3-32B\n919\t    - Δ\n920\t    rows:\n921\t    - - C1 Disagree Rate\n922\t      - 52.0%\n923\t      - 39.6%\n924\t      - +12.4pp\n925\t    - - C2 Precision\n926\t      - 61.0%\n927\t      - 86.8%\n928\t      - -25.8pp\n929\t    - - C4 Δ All-mode\n930\t      - +1.5pp\n931\t      - +5.2pp\n932\t      - -3.7pp\n933\t    - - C5 Localization\n934\t      - 68.0%\n935\t      - 85.4%\n936\t      - -17.4pp\n937\t    - - FOL:Code Error Ratio\n938\t      - '4:1'\n939\t      - '9:1'\n940\t      - Asymmetry reduced\n941\t    - - Both-Wrong Rate\n942\t      - 28.0%\n943\t      - ~10%\n944\t      - +18pp\n945\t    - - FOL Crash Rate\n946\t      - 12.0%\n947\t      - ~2%\n948\t      - +10pp\n949\t  figures_description:\n950\t  - 'Scatter: model capability (8B vs 32B) on x-axis, disagree rate vs diagnostic\n951\t    precision on y-axis, showing inverse relationship — more disagreement but less\n952\t    informative'\n953\t  analysis: '8B 结果揭示了 cross-representation diagnosis 的另一个 applicability condition：\n954\t    模型能力需要足够高，使得至少一种表征是 reliable 的。当模型能力不足时，both-wrong rate 上升，分歧变成噪声。这支持 \"asymmetric\n955\t    reliability\" 作为 necessary condition 的论点。 在 reframed narrative 中，这与 MATH 的 failure\n956\t    mode 形成呼应——无论是因为 domain （MATH 中 CoT 和 SymPy 都 fallible）还是因为 model capability（8B\n957\t    中 FOL 也不可靠）， 一旦 asymmetric reliability 被打破，diagnosis 就失效。\n958\t\n959\t    '\n960\t- name: GPQA Diamond Extension\n961\t  plan_id: exp-011\n962\t  description: 科学知识推理领域，CoT vs Python 验证代码\n963\t  expected_results:\n964\t    N_samples: 150\n965\t    C1_disagree_rate: 0.11\n966\t    C2_diagnostic_precision: 0.56\n967\t    C4_delta_pp: -1.8\n968\t    C5_localization_accuracy: 0.6\n969\t    cot_code_error_ratio: 1.3:1\n970\t    correlated_failure_rate: 0.38\n971\t    code_not_applicable_rate: 0.35\n972\t    mvp_pass_count: 0/5\n973\t  result_rationale: 'GPQA Diamond 是 worst-case 的极端表现。disagree rate 仅 11%，precision\n974\t    56%（接近随机）。 核心原因：科学推理（物理/化学/生物）中 Python 代码的角色与逻辑域完全不同——大部分 GPQA 问题 需要 domain knowledge\n975\t    和 conceptual reasoning，Python 只能验证计算步骤但无法验证 conceptual correctness。35% 的问题 Code\n976\t    表征 \"不适用\"（无法有意义地用代码验证）。 CoT:Code error ratio 几乎对称（1.3:1），完全丧失了逻辑域的 asymmetric reliability。\n977\t    Correlated failure rate 高达 38%——模型在科学知识上的盲点在两种表征上都表现出来。 C4 为负——targeted repair\n978\t    不如 blind，因为 \"diagnosis\" 信息在科学域几乎没有 actionability。\n979\t\n980\t    '\n981\t  tables:\n982\t  - table_id: tab-exp011-1\n983\t    caption: GPQA Diamond Results (N=150, Qwen3-32B)\n984\t    columns:\n985\t    - Metric\n986\t    - GPQA\n987\t    - MATH\n988\t    - FOLIO\n989\t    rows:\n990\t    - - C1 Disagree Rate\n991\t      - 11.0%\n992\t      - 14.0%\n993\t      - 39.6%\n994\t    - - C2 Precision\n995\t      - 56.0%\n996\t      - 58.3%\n997\t      - 86.8%\n998\t    - - C4 Δ\n999\t      - -1.8pp\n1000\t      - -0.5pp\n1001\t      - +5.2pp\n1002\t    - - C5 Localization\n1003\t      - 60.0%\n1004\t      - 63.0%\n1005\t      - 85.4%\n1006\t    - - Error Ratio\n1007\t      - 1.3:1\n1008\t      - 1.8:1\n1009\t      - '9:1'\n1010\t    - - Correlated Failure%\n1011\t      - 38.0%\n1012\t      - 31.0%\n1013\t      - 18.2%\n1014\t    - - Code N/A Rate\n1015\t      - 35.0%\n1016\t      - 8.0%\n1017\t      - 0%\n1018\t  figures_description:\n1019\t  - 'Gradient heatmap: 4 benchmarks (FOLIO → ProofWriter → MATH → GPQA) showing monotonic\n1020\t    degradation of all metrics, establishing the applicability spectrum'\n1021\t  analysis: GPQA 完成了 \"applicability spectrum\" 的构建：FOLIO（强信号）→ ProofWriter（弱信号）→ MATH（噪声）→\n1022\t    GPQA（失效）。关键维度是 representation asymmetry 和 formalization-vs-knowledge error ratio。GPQA\n1023\t    的 35% code-not-applicable rate 揭示了一个 fundamental limitation： cross-representation\n1024\t    diagnosis 要求两种表征都能 meaningfully encode the reasoning， 而科学推理中 Code 常常只能部分覆盖推理过程。\n1025\t    这在 reframed narrative 中作为 applicability conditions 的最外层边界。\n1026\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3e779216-cbf6-4585-b15e-4c991e2c88e5","uuid":"570c38ec-72a5-46e4-9679-e8fdb7ec7229","timestamp":"2026-05-15T06:48:33.101Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_3/projects/cross_representation_disagreement_diagno/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T060408/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '放弃 ''general cross-representation diagnosis framework'' 的普适性叙事。Reframe\n  为 domain-specific 深度研究：''When and Why Cross-Representation Disagreement Works: A\n  Case Study in Formal Logic Reasoning''。核心 angle 转向：(1) 深度刻画 FOL-Code 分歧在逻辑推理中的独特有效性及其认知/结构原因，\n  (2) 系统性分析跨域失败的原因（correlated failures、specification-level errors 的普遍性）， (3) 提出 cross-representation\n  diagnosis 的 applicability conditions。用深度补广度，FOLIO 上 的分析必须足够深。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Cross-Model Ablation (FOLIO)\n  plan_id: exp-002\n  description: DeepSeek V4 Pro 生成一种表征 + Qwen3-32B 生成另一种，测试模型多样性是否降低 correlated failures\n  expected_results:\n    C1_disagree_rate_mixed: 0.42\n    C1_disagree_rate_deepseek_only: 0.33\n    C2_diagnostic_precision_mixed: 0.83\n    C2_diagnostic_precision_deepseek_only: 0.78\n    false_agreement_reduction_vs_single_model_pp: 1.5\n    correlated_failure_rate_single_model: 0.18\n    correlated_failure_rate_mixed_model: 0.165\n    C5_localization_mixed: 0.81\n    new_disagreement_type_introduced: true\n    spurious_disagreement_rate_mixed: 0.09\n  result_rationale: '混合模型配置仅将 false agreement 降低约 1.5pp（从 ~18% 到 ~16.5%），远低于预期的 5-8pp。\n    原因：correlated failures 的根源不在于 \"同一个模型的 shared bias\"，而在于 specification-level ambiguity——两个不同模型面对同一道模糊\n    NL 问题时，犯相同的 specification error 的概率仍然很高， 因为错误来源是 NL 本身的歧义而非模型内部表征。DeepSeek V4\n    Pro 单独运行时 disagree rate 更低（33% vs 39.6%），说明更强模型的两种表征更趋一致（能力提升同时减少了 formalization-specific\n    errors 和 diagnostic opportunities）。混合模型引入约 9% 的 spurious disagreements——两个模型对\n    同一问题的合法但不同的形式化选择（如变量命名、逻辑等价变换），这些分歧不是 errors 而是 representation divergence，降低了整体\n    precision。结论：模型多样性不是解决 correlated failures 的有效路径， 因为 correlation 的主要来源是 task specification\n    而非 model bias。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - table_id: tab-exp002-1\n    caption: Cross-Model vs Single-Model Pipeline Comparison (FOLIO, N=192)\n    columns:\n    - Config\n    - C1 Disagree%\n    - C2 Precision%\n    - Correlated Failure%\n    - Spurious Disagree%\n    - C5 Localization%\n    rows:\n    - - Qwen3-32B (single)\n      - 39.6%\n      - 86.8%\n      - 18.2%\n      - 3.1%\n      - 85.4%\n    - - DeepSeek V4 Pro (single)\n      - 33.3%\n      - 78.1%\n      - 19.8%\n      - 4.2%\n      - 79.7%\n    - - Mixed (DS-FOL, Qwen-Code)\n      - 42.2%\n      - 83.3%\n      - 16.5%\n      - 9.1%\n      - 81.3%\n    - - Mixed (Qwen-FOL, DS-Code)\n      - 40.6%\n      - 80.6%\n      - 17.1%\n      - 8.7%\n      - 78.9%\n  - table_id: tab-exp002-2\n    caption: False Agreement Breakdown by Error Source\n    columns:\n    - Error Source\n    - Single-Model False Agree%\n    - Mixed-Model False Agree%\n    - Δ\n    rows:\n    - - Specification-level ambiguity\n      - 11.5%\n      - 10.9%\n      - -0.6pp\n    - - Shared formalization bias\n      - 4.2%\n      - 3.1%\n      - -1.1pp\n    - - Independent coincidental\n      - 2.5%\n      - 2.5%\n      - 0.0pp\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Venn diagram: Qwen-only failures vs DeepSeek-only failures vs shared failures,\n    showing ~70% overlap in false-agreement samples across models — evidence that\n    correlated failures are task-driven not model-driven'\n  - 'Bar chart: spurious disagreement rate by disagreement category (legitimate formalization\n    choice vs actual error), showing mixed-model introduces ~3x more spurious disagreements'\n  analysis: '核心发现是 correlated failures 的主要来源是 task specification 而非 model bias，因此\n    cross-model 策略的边际收益极小。这对 general framework 叙事是重大打击——如果 false agreement 无法通过模型多样性有效缓解，那么\n    diagnosis coverage 存在固有上限。但这一 negative result 本身 具有 insight 价值：它揭示了 cross-representation\n    diagnosis 的 fundamental limitation 来自 NL-to-formal 的 specification gap，而非模型能力。在\n    reframed narrative 中，这成为 boundary characterization 的关键 evidence。\n\n    '\n- name: ProofWriter Extension\n  plan_id: exp-003\n  description: 在 ProofWriter 上运行完整 pipeline，验证逻辑推理域内泛化性\n  expected_results:\n    N_samples: 300\n    C1_disagree_rate: 0.17\n    C2_diagnostic_precision: 0.63\n    C3_error_types: 2\n    C4_targeted_vs_blind_delta_pp_all_mode: 1.8\n    C4_targeted_vs_blind_delta_pp_excl_unknown: -2.1\n    C5_localization_accuracy: 0.72\n    fol_code_error_ratio: '7:1'\n    mvp_pass_count: 2/5 (C1 borderline FAIL at <20% threshold pending, C2 FAIL, C3\n      PASS, C4 FAIL, C5 PASS)\n    bootstrap_C1_95CI:\n    - 0.13\n    - 0.22\n    bootstrap_C2_95CI:\n    - 0.54\n    - 0.71\n    fisher_exact_C4_p_value: 0.31\n  result_rationale: 'ProofWriter 的 disagree rate 仅 17%，远低于 FOLIO 的 39.6%。根本原因：ProofWriter\n    的问题 结构高度规范化——前提以 \"If X then Y\" 的固定模板给出，推理深度可控（depth 0-5），NL 歧义极少。 这意味着 LLM 在 FOL\n    和 Code 两种表征上都能较准确地捕获 specification，formalization-specific errors 的发生率本身就低。剩余的\n    17% 分歧中，diagnostic precision 降至 63%：更多分歧来自 \"两种表征对 closed-world assumption 的不同处理\"——FOL/Z3\n    默认 CWA 而 Python 代码常遗漏 CWA 导致的推理差异，这类分歧是 representation semantics gap 而非 formalization\n    error。 error types 仅 2 种（缺少 FOLIO 上的 \"scope ambiguity\" 类型，因为 ProofWriter 无量词 作用域歧义）。Repair\n    delta 仅 1.8pp（All-mode），因为可诊断的 errors 本身就少，且 CWA-related 分歧不可通过 repair 单侧修复。Excl-Unknown\n    为负（-2.1pp），因为 ProofWriter 无 Unknown 类别，所有样本都是 True/False，移除了 FOLIO 上驱动 repair\n    delta 的主要子集。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - table_id: tab-exp003-1\n    caption: ProofWriter Full Pipeline Results (N=300, Qwen3-32B)\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - ProofWriter\n    - FOLIO (reference)\n    - Δ\n    rows:\n    - - C1 Disagree Rate\n      - 17.0% (42/247)\n      - 39.6% (76/192)\n      - -22.6pp\n    - - C2 Diagnostic Precision\n      - 63.2% (24/38)\n      - 86.8% (66/76)\n      - -23.6pp\n    - - C3 Error Types\n      - '2'\n      - '3'\n      - '-1'\n    - - C4 Δ (All-mode)\n      - +1.8pp\n      - +5.2pp\n      - -3.4pp\n    - - C4 Δ (Excl-Unknown)\n      - -2.1pp\n      - +0.0pp\n      - -2.1pp\n    - - C5 Localization\n      - 72.0%\n      - 85.4%\n      - -13.4pp\n  - table_id: tab-exp003-2\n    caption: 'Disagreement Source Analysis: ProofWriter vs FOLIO'\n    columns:\n    - Disagreement Source\n    - ProofWriter %\n    - FOLIO %\n    rows:\n    - - Formalization-specific error (one side wrong)\n      - 63.2%\n      - 86.8%\n    - - CWA/semantic gap (neither side truly wrong)\n      - 26.3%\n      - 5.3%\n    - - Both sides wrong (correlated failure)\n      - 10.5%\n      - 7.9%\n  - table_id: tab-exp003-3\n    caption: ProofWriter Results by Reasoning Depth\n    columns:\n    - Depth\n    - N\n    - Disagree%\n    - Precision%\n    - Notes\n    rows:\n    - - '0'\n      - '62'\n      - 8.1%\n      - 40.0%\n      - Trivial problems, few errors to detect\n    - - '1'\n      - '68'\n      - 13.2%\n      - 55.6%\n      - Simple chain, low formalization difficulty\n    - - '2'\n      - '58'\n      - 17.2%\n      - 66.7%\n      - Moderate depth\n    - - '3'\n      - '52'\n      - 23.1%\n      - 70.0%\n      - More complex chains increase error rate\n    - - '5'\n      - '60'\n      - 26.7%\n      - 75.0%\n      - Deepest reasoning shows highest signal\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Line plot: disagree rate and diagnostic precision vs reasoning depth (0-5), showing\n    monotonic increase — signal improves with task complexity but even depth-5 falls\n    below FOLIO baseline'\n  - 'Confusion matrix: FOL vs Code correctness on ProofWriter, showing the 7:1 asymmetry\n    persists but both sides are more accurate overall (fewer errors = fewer disagreements)'\n  analysis: 'ProofWriter 结果确认了 worst-case 假设：诊断信号在结构化程度更高的 benchmark 上显著退化。 disagree\n    rate 仅 17% 且 precision 仅 63%，均低于 FOLIO。关键 insight：cross-representation disagreement\n    的 informativeness 与 NL specification 的 ambiguity 正相关——ProofWriter 的 \"clean\" NL\n    减少了 formalization errors，但也减少了 diagnostic opportunities。 这不是方法的失败，而是 applicability\n    boundary：当 NL→formal 翻译足够 straightforward 时，cross-representation diagnosis 的附加价值有限。depth-5\n    子集数据（26.7% disagree, 75% precision）暗示在更难的推理链上信号恢复，为 \"complexity threshold\" 的 boundary\n    condition 提供了 evidence。Reframed narrative 中，ProofWriter 作为 \"lower boundary\" 与\n    FOLIO 的 \"sweet spot\" 形成对照。\n\n    '\n- name: MATH Level 5 Extension\n  plan_id: exp-004\n  description: 在 MATH 难题子集运行 CoT vs SymPy/Python 双表征 pipeline\n  expected_results:\n    N_samples: 200\n    C1_disagree_rate: 0.14\n    C2_diagnostic_precision: 0.58\n    C3_error_types: 3\n    C4_targeted_vs_blind_delta_pp_all_mode: -0.5\n    C4_targeted_vs_blind_delta_pp_excl_unknown: -3.2\n    C5_localization_accuracy: 0.63\n    cot_sympy_error_ratio: 1.8:1\n    fol_code_error_ratio_equivalent: 7.2\n    mvp_pass_count: 0/5 (all FAIL)\n    bootstrap_C1_95CI:\n    - 0.09\n    - 0.19\n    bootstrap_C2_95CI:\n    - 0.47\n    - 0.68\n    fisher_exact_C4_p_value: 0.82\n    correlated_failure_rate: 0.31\n    specification_error_rate: 0.24\n  result_rationale: 'MATH 域的双表征分歧模式与逻辑域本质不同，不支持统一框架叙事。核心原因有三： (1) 错误对称性逆转——CoT:SymPy\n    error ratio 仅 1.8:1，远低于 FOLIO 的 9:1。数学推理中 CoT 的自然语言链式推导和 SymPy 的符号计算犯错概率更接近，因为数学\n    errors 更多是 \"计算错误\" 而非 \"形式化翻译错误\"。FOL 在逻辑域近乎 \"ground truth\" 的角色（因为 Z3 solver 的完备性）\n    在数学域不成立——SymPy 无法解决所有数学问题类型（如几何、组合），常 fallback 到数值近似。 (2) Correlated failure rate\n    高达 31%——MATH Level 5 的难度意味着模型在 CoT 和 SymPy 两条路径上都无法正确 specify 问题（如组合恒等式、复杂积分），产生大量\n    false agreement（双方 都错但碰巧同一答案或都无法执行）。 (3) 分歧的 diagnostic content 不同——MATH 上的分歧更多反映\n    \"能否用该表征解决此类问题\" （capability mismatch）而非 \"形式化翻译是否正确\"（formalization quality）。例如 SymPy\n    无法处理某些几何题，不是 formalization error 而是 tool limitation。 这导致 C2 precision 仅 58%，C5\n    localization 仅 63%（因为 \"错误侧\" 的判定不明确—— 可能两侧都有道理但方法不同），repair delta 为负（targeted repair\n    反而引入 noise）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - table_id: tab-exp004-1\n    caption: MATH Level 5 Full Pipeline Results (N=200, Qwen3-32B)\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - MATH\n    - FOLIO (ref)\n    - ProofWriter (ref)\n    rows:\n    - - C1 Disagree Rate\n      - 14.0% (24/172)\n      - 39.6%\n      - 17.0%\n    - - C2 Diagnostic Precision\n      - 58.3% (14/24)\n      - 86.8%\n      - 63.2%\n    - - C3 Error Types\n      - '3'\n      - '3'\n      - '2'\n    - - C4 Δ All-mode\n      - -0.5pp\n      - +5.2pp\n      - +1.8pp\n    - - C4 Δ Excl-Unk\n      - -3.2pp\n      - +0.0pp\n      - -2.1pp\n    - - C5 Localization\n      - 63.0%\n      - 85.4%\n      - 72.0%\n    - - Error Ratio (logic:code equiv)\n      - 1.8:1\n      - '9:1'\n      - '7:1'\n    - - Correlated Failure Rate\n      - 31.0%\n      - 18.2%\n      - 10.5%\n  - table_id: tab-exp004-2\n    caption: MATH Disagreement Source by Problem Category\n    columns:\n    - MATH Category\n    - N\n    - Disagree%\n    - Precision%\n    - CoT:SymPy Error Ratio\n    rows:\n    - - Algebra\n      - '52'\n      - 17.3%\n      - 71.4%\n      - 2.5:1\n    - - Number Theory\n      - '38'\n      - 15.8%\n      - 60.0%\n      - 2.0:1\n    - - Counting & Prob\n      - '35'\n      - 11.4%\n      - 50.0%\n      - 1.5:1\n    - - Geometry\n      - '28'\n      - 10.7%\n      - 33.3%\n      - 1.0:1\n    - - Precalculus\n      - '25'\n      - 12.0%\n      - 50.0%\n      - 1.2:1\n    - - Intermediate Algebra\n      - '22'\n      - 18.2%\n      - 66.7%\n      - 2.2:1\n  - table_id: tab-exp004-3\n    caption: 'Error Type Distribution: MATH vs Logic Domains'\n    columns:\n    - Error Type\n    - MATH %\n    - FOLIO %\n    - Interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - Formalization-specific\n      - 33%\n      - 72%\n      - Much less dominant in MATH\n    - - Specification-level\n      - 24%\n      - 10%\n      - NL→formal ambiguity higher in MATH\n    - - Tool limitation\n      - 28%\n      - 0%\n      - SymPy can't solve certain problem types\n    - - Computational error\n      - 15%\n      - 18%\n      - Similar across domains\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter plot: CoT accuracy vs SymPy accuracy per MATH category, showing near-diagonal\n    clustering (error ratio ~1.8:1) vs FOLIO''s extreme off-diagonal (9:1) — the asymmetry\n    that makes diagnosis work in logic does not exist in math'\n  - 'Stacked bar: error source distribution across three benchmarks (FOLIO/ProofWriter/MATH),\n    showing formalization-specific errors declining from 72% to 33% while specification-level\n    and tool-limitation errors grow'\n  - 'Heatmap: false agreement rate by MATH difficulty sublevel and category, showing\n    concentrated failure in geometry and combinatorics'\n  analysis: 'MATH 结果是 worst-case 的核心 evidence。0/5 MVP pass 意味着 cross-representation\n    diagnosis 在数学域基本失效。关键 insight：诊断方法的有效性依赖于两种表征之间的 \"asymmetric reliability\"——在逻辑域，Z3\n    的完备性保证了 FOL 侧几乎总是对的，使分歧成为高质量的 error detector。数学域缺少这种 asymmetry：CoT 和 SymPy 都是\n    \"fallible solvers\"，分歧不再指向 \"哪边错了\"而是 \"两种方法对此题的适用性不同\"。Tool limitation（28%）作为新 error\n    type 出现，这类错误不可通过 repair 修复（SymPy 本身不支持的问题类型）。 在 reframed narrative 中，这构成了 \"applicability\n    condition\" 的核心论据： cross-representation diagnosis requires asymmetric reliability\n    between representations， 而这在 formal logic 域自然成立（Z3 completeness）但在其他域不保证。\n\n    '\n- name: Repair Mechanism Improvement\n  plan_id: exp-005\n  description: 多轮 repair + 错误类型特定修复策略，尝试拉大 targeted vs blind 差距\n  expected_results:\n    C4_round1_delta_pp_all_mode: 5.2\n    C4_round2_delta_pp_all_mode: 2.6\n    C4_round3_delta_pp_all_mode: 2.1\n    C4_improved_prompt_delta_pp_all_mode: 3.0\n    C4_best_config_delta_pp_all_mode: 3.0\n    C4_best_config_delta_pp_excl_unknown: -1.5\n    repair_success_rate_formalization_errors: 0.22\n    repair_success_rate_specification_errors: 0.04\n    multi_round_diminishing_returns: true\n    error_type_specific_vs_generic_delta: 0.8\n  result_rationale: '多轮 repair 和改进 prompt 均未能突破 C4 delta 瓶颈。原因分析： (1) 多轮 repair 呈显著递减收益——Round\n    1 的 5.2pp 到 Round 2 降至 2.6pp，Round 3 仅 2.1pp。这是因为 Round 1 已修复了 \"easy fixes\"（简单的语法级\n    formalization errors）， 剩余的 errors 是 deep semantic misunderstandings（模型对 NL 含义的理解偏差），多轮\n    regeneration 不改变模型的理解。 (2) 改进 prompt（加入 error type 信息）的 delta 反而降至 3.0pp——更详细的\n    diagnosis 信息有时误导 repair：当 error type classification 本身有 ~15% 错误率时，提供错误的 error\n    type 信息比不提供更差。 (3) Excl-Unknown 从 0.0pp 恶化到 -1.5pp——多轮 repair 在 True/False 样本上引入了\n    regression（过度修改导致原本正确的逻辑被破坏）。 (4) 核心瓶颈：repair 只能修复 formalization-specific errors（22%\n    成功率），对 specification-level errors 几乎无效（4%），而后者占 errors 的 ~30%。targeted repair\n    的上限被 error type 分布锁定。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - table_id: tab-exp005-1\n    caption: Multi-Round Repair Results (FOLIO, N=96 disagreement pairs)\n    columns:\n    - Config\n    - Targeted Acc\n    - Blind Acc\n    - Δ (pp)\n    - Excl-Unk Δ (pp)\n    rows:\n    - - Baseline (Round 1, original prompt)\n      - 63.5%\n      - 58.3%\n      - '+5.2'\n      - '+0.0'\n    - - Round 2 (re-repair failures)\n      - 64.6%\n      - 62.0%\n      - '+2.6'\n      - '-0.5'\n    - - Round 3 (re-repair failures)\n      - 65.1%\n      - 63.0%\n      - '+2.1'\n      - '-1.0'\n    - - Improved prompt (error-type-specific)\n      - 62.5%\n      - 59.5%\n      - '+3.0'\n      - '-1.5'\n    - - Best combo (Round 2 + improved)\n      - 63.8%\n      - 60.8%\n      - '+3.0'\n      - '-1.5'\n  - table_id: tab-exp005-2\n    caption: Repair Success Rate by Error Type\n    columns:\n    - Error Type\n    - N (targeted)\n    - Repair Success%\n    - Blind Success%\n    - Δ\n    rows:\n    - - Variable mapping error\n      - '18'\n      - 33.3%\n      - 22.2%\n      - +11.1pp\n    - - Scope/quantifier error\n      - '12'\n      - 16.7%\n      - 16.7%\n      - +0.0pp\n    - - Logic connective error\n      - '15'\n      - 26.7%\n      - 20.0%\n      - +6.7pp\n    - - Specification-level error\n      - '9'\n      - 4.4%\n      - 6.7%\n      - -2.2pp\n    - - Unknown GT (all errors)\n      - '42'\n      - 28.6%\n      - 19.0%\n      - +9.5pp\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Line plot: C4 delta (pp) across repair rounds (1-3), showing monotonic decrease\n    — diminishing returns curve with inflection at Round 1'\n  - 'Grouped bar chart: repair success rate by error type for targeted vs blind, showing\n    targeted advantage concentrates on variable-mapping and logic-connective errors\n    while specification errors show no benefit'\n  analysis: 'Repair improvement 实验确认了 C4 delta 的 structural ceiling。最佳配置仅 3.0pp All-mode（低于\n    MVP 的 5.2pp，因为 improved prompt 有时误导），Excl-Unknown 为负。 这是 worst-case 的关键：即使投入 3\n    rounds repair + error-type-specific prompts， targeted repair 相比 blind 的优势依然 marginal。根本原因是\n    diagnosis 信息对 repair 的 actionability 有限——知道 \"Code 侧有 variable mapping error\" 并不能帮助\n    LLM 在 重新生成时避免同样的错误，因为错误来源于 LLM 对 NL 语义的理解而非生成随机性。 在 reframed narrative 中，这支持 \"diagnosis\n    as analysis tool, not repair tool\" 的定位。\n\n    '\n- name: Unknown Sample Deep Analysis\n  plan_id: exp-006\n  description: 分析 GT=Unknown 样本为何驱动 C4 delta，探索 specification-level vs formalization-specific\n    差异\n  expected_results:\n    unknown_sample_count: 66\n    unknown_disagree_rate: 0.47\n    unknown_specification_error_rate: 0.08\n    unknown_formalization_error_rate: 0.39\n    true_false_specification_error_rate: 0.22\n    true_false_formalization_error_rate: 0.14\n    unknown_fol_code_error_ratio: '12:1'\n    true_false_fol_code_error_ratio: '6:1'\n    unknown_repair_delta_pp: 9.5\n    true_false_repair_delta_pp: -1.7\n  result_rationale: 'Unknown 样本驱动 C4 delta 的原因在 worst-case 下被揭示为一个 confound 而非 feature：\n    (1) Unknown 样本的 FOL:Code asymmetry 更极端（12:1 vs 6:1）——Z3 solver 对 \"信息不足\" 的判定（返回\n    Unknown）几乎总是正确的，而 Python 代码极难正确实现 \"三值逻辑\"（True/False/Unknown）， 倾向于错误地返回 True 或\n    False。这不是 \"diagnosis 发现了 formalization error\" 而是 \"Code 表征在结构上不适合处理 Unknown 类别\"。\n    (2) True/False 样本的 specification error rate 更高（22% vs 8%），因为需要完整的 逻辑推理链，任何 NL\n    歧义都传播为 specification error。Unknown 样本通常只需检测 \"信息不足\"， specification 更简单。 (3) 这意味着\n    FOLIO 上的 C4 success 本质上是 \"Z3 对 Unknown 判定的优越性\" 的 side effect， 而非 cross-representation\n    diagnosis 的 general 能力。当移除 Unknown 样本后 C4 delta 消失 就是这个 confound 的直接证据。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - table_id: tab-exp006-1\n    caption: 'Error Mode Distribution: Unknown vs True/False Samples'\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - GT=Unknown (N=66)\n    - GT=True/False (N=126)\n    - Interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - Disagree Rate\n      - 47.0%\n      - 35.7%\n      - Unknown samples produce more disagreement\n    - - Specification Error Rate\n      - 8.1%\n      - 22.2%\n      - True/False problems have more NL ambiguity\n    - - Formalization Error Rate\n      - 39.4%\n      - 14.3%\n      - Unknown triggers Code-side errors\n    - - FOL:Code Error Ratio\n      - '12:1'\n      - '6:1'\n      - Extreme asymmetry on Unknown\n    - - Code 'Unknown' output rate\n      - 12.1%\n      - N/A\n      - Code rarely outputs Unknown correctly\n    - - Repair Δ (targeted vs blind)\n      - +9.5pp\n      - -1.7pp\n      - Entire C4 signal from Unknown\n  - table_id: tab-exp006-2\n    caption: Code-side Error Patterns on Unknown Samples\n    columns:\n    - Code Output\n    - Count\n    - '%'\n    - Is Error?\n    rows:\n    - - True (should be Unknown)\n      - '18'\n      - 58.1%\n      - Yes — most common failure\n    - - False (should be Unknown)\n      - '9'\n      - 29.0%\n      - 'Yes'\n    - - Unknown (correct)\n      - '3'\n      - 9.7%\n      - 'No'\n    - - Runtime Error\n      - '1'\n      - 3.2%\n      - 'Yes'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Stacked bar: error type distribution split by GT label (Unknown / True / False),\n    showing formalization errors dominate Unknown while specification errors dominate\n    True/False'\n  - 'Decision tree visualization: why Unknown samples are ''easy'' for diagnosis —\n    Z3 returns Unknown → almost certainly correct → any Code disagreement is Code-side\n    error → repair = regenerate Code'\n  analysis: '这个分析在 worst-case scenario 中具有双刃剑效应。一方面，它解释了 C4 delta 的来源并揭示了 一个重要的 confound：FOLIO\n    上的 repair success 主要来自 Unknown 样本中 Code 表征对三值逻辑 的结构性缺陷，而非 diagnosis 的 general\n    能力。另一方面，在 reframed narrative 中，这恰好 是 \"When and Why\" 的深度案例：精确刻画了 WHY diagnosis\n    works（Z3 completeness + representation asymmetry）和 WHEN it fails（True/False samples\n    where specification errors dominate）。这个 confound 的发现本身是 contribution——它警告后续研究者\n    cross-representation diagnosis 的效果可能被特定 GT label 分布所夸大。\n\n    '\n- name: Selection vs Repair Ablation\n  plan_id: exp-007\n  description: 检测到分歧后，直接选择另一侧 vs 诊断引导修复的对比\n  expected_results:\n    selection_accuracy_all_mode: 0.68\n    repair_accuracy_all_mode: 0.635\n    selection_vs_repair_delta_pp: 4.5\n    selection_accuracy_excl_unknown: 0.61\n    repair_accuracy_excl_unknown: 0.59\n    selection_accuracy_when_localization_correct: 0.8\n    selection_accuracy_when_localization_wrong: 0.31\n    oracle_selection_accuracy: 0.88\n  result_rationale: 'Selection（直接选正确侧）在 All-mode 上以 4.5pp 优于 Repair（68% vs 63.5%），这对\n    repair contribution 是直接打击。原因： (1) 在 9:1 的 FOL:Code asymmetry 下，\"永远选 FOL\" 这个 naive\n    策略本身就有 ~90% 的 accuracy on disagreement samples。Selection with localization（选 localization\n    判定的 正确侧）达到 68%（受限于 localization 的 85% accuracy——当 localization 错误时 selection 反而选了错误侧，降至\n    31%）。 (2) Repair 的 63.5% 低于 selection 的 68%，因为 repair 引入了 regeneration noise——\n    即使 diagnosis 正确指出了错误侧和错误类型，LLM 的重新生成不保证修复该错误，有时甚至引入新错误。 (3) Oracle selection（假设\n    perfect localization）达到 88%，说明 localization accuracy 是 selection 策略的主要瓶颈。这暗示 \"提升\n    localization\" 比 \"提升 repair\" 更有杠杆。 在 worst-case 下，这意味着 repair 作为 downstream application\n    不仅 marginal 而且 不如更简单的 selection baseline。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - table_id: tab-exp007-1\n    caption: Selection vs Repair Comparison (FOLIO disagreement samples)\n    columns:\n    - Strategy\n    - All-mode Acc\n    - Excl-Unk Acc\n    - Compute Cost (relative)\n    rows:\n    - - Always-FOL baseline\n      - 65.8%\n      - 57.8%\n      - 0x (no extra)\n    - - Selection (w/ localization)\n      - 68.0%\n      - 61.0%\n      - 0x (no extra)\n    - - Repair (targeted, 1 round)\n      - 63.5%\n      - 59.3%\n      - 1x (regeneration)\n    - - Repair (targeted, 3 rounds)\n      - 65.1%\n      - 57.6%\n      - 3x\n    - - Oracle Selection\n      - 88.0%\n      - 82.0%\n      - 0x (hypothetical)\n    - - Blind Repair (1 round)\n      - 58.3%\n      - 59.3%\n      - 1x\n  - table_id: tab-exp007-2\n    caption: Selection Accuracy Conditioned on Localization Correctness\n    columns:\n    - Localization\n    - N\n    - Selection Acc\n    - Repair Acc\n    rows:\n    - - Correct (85.4%)\n      - '35'\n      - 80.0%\n      - 68.6%\n    - - Incorrect (14.6%)\n      - '6'\n      - 31.3%\n      - 50.0%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart with error bars: accuracy comparison across 5 strategies (always-FOL,\n    selection, repair-1, repair-3, oracle-selection), showing selection > repair and\n    oracle-selection sets the ceiling'\n  - 'Scatter: per-sample selection outcome vs repair outcome, showing weak correlation\n    (r=0.32) — selection and repair succeed on different subsets'\n  analysis: 'Selection > Repair 的结果在 worst-case 中直接质疑了 repair 作为 downstream application\n    的价值。一个更简单、零额外计算成本的策略（selection）beats 更复杂、需要额外 LLM call 的策略 （repair），这在 reviewer\n    眼中是 fatal weakness for the repair narrative。然而在 reframed narrative 中，这反而支持 \"diagnosis\n    as analysis, not repair\" 的定位：cross-representation disagreement 的价值在于 detection\n    和 localization，不在于 repair。Selection 的成功 恰好证明 diagnosis 的上游价值（localization accuracy\n    直接决定 selection quality）。 Oracle selection 88% 的上限暗示未来方向：提升 localization 精度是 highest-leverage\n    improvement。\n\n    '\n- name: Error Taxonomy Ablation\n  plan_id: exp-008\n  description: 按错误类型分派修复策略 vs 固定策略的对比\n  expected_results:\n    taxonomy_guided_repair_acc: 0.625\n    fixed_strategy_repair_acc: 0.615\n    taxonomy_vs_fixed_delta_pp: 1.0\n    taxonomy_guided_by_error_type:\n      variable_mapping: 0.333\n      scope_quantifier: 0.167\n      logic_connective: 0.267\n    fixed_strategy_by_error_type:\n      variable_mapping: 0.278\n      scope_quantifier: 0.167\n      logic_connective: 0.2\n    taxonomy_misclassification_rate: 0.15\n    taxonomy_misclassification_repair_success: 0.07\n  result_rationale: 'Taxonomy-guided repair 仅比 fixed strategy 高 1.0pp（62.5% vs 61.5%），在\n    worst-case 下这个差异统计不显著（p=0.68, Fisher exact test）。原因： (1) Error taxonomy 的分类准确率约\n    85%，那 15% 的 misclassification 会导致错误的修复策略 被应用，反而降低 repair 效果——misclassified samples\n    的 repair 成功率仅 7%（vs correctly classified 的 ~25%）。 (2) 不同 error type 的最优修复策略差异不大——无论是\n    variable mapping error 还是 logic connective error，LLM 的 repair 本质上都是 \"重新生成并希望这次不犯同样的错\"。Error\n    type 信息对 repair prompt 的 marginal guidance 有限，因为 LLM 不能精确执行 \"只修改变量映射 而保持其他逻辑不变\"\n    这样的指令。 (3) Scope/quantifier errors 在两种策略下 repair 成功率相同（16.7%），说明这类 deep semantic\n    errors 超出了 prompt-level repair 的能力边界。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - table_id: tab-exp008-1\n    caption: Taxonomy-Guided vs Fixed Strategy Repair (FOLIO)\n    columns:\n    - Strategy\n    - Overall Acc\n    - Variable Map\n    - Scope/Quant\n    - Logic Conn\n    - p-value\n    rows:\n    - - Taxonomy-guided\n      - 62.5%\n      - 33.3%\n      - 16.7%\n      - 26.7%\n      - ''\n    - - Fixed (generic regen)\n      - 61.5%\n      - 27.8%\n      - 16.7%\n      - 20.0%\n      - '0.68'\n    - - Δ\n      - +1.0pp\n      - +5.5pp\n      - +0.0pp\n      - +6.7pp\n      - n.s.\n  - table_id: tab-exp008-2\n    caption: Impact of Taxonomy Misclassification on Repair\n    columns:\n    - Classification\n    - N\n    - Repair Success%\n    - Notes\n    rows:\n    - - Correctly classified\n      - '36'\n      - 25.0%\n      - Taxonomy info slightly helps\n    - - Misclassified\n      - '5'\n      - 7.1%\n      - Wrong repair strategy applied\n    - - All targeted\n      - '41'\n      - 22.0%\n      - Weighted average\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Grouped bar: repair success rate per error type, taxonomy-guided vs fixed, with\n    95% CI error bars overlapping on all types'\n  - 'Sankey diagram: error type classification → repair strategy → outcome, showing\n    misclassification paths leading to failures'\n  analysis: 'Taxonomy 的规定性价值在 worst-case 下几乎不存在。1.0pp 的差异在 N=41 的样本量下统计不显著， 无法 claim\n    taxonomy-guided repair is better than generic repair。这对论文的 error taxonomy contribution\n    有影响——如果 taxonomy 只有 descriptive value（帮助理解 errors） 而无 prescriptive value（指导 repair），reviewer\n    可能质疑 taxonomy 的实用性。 在 reframed narrative 中，taxonomy 的价值重新定位为 analytical tool：它帮助解释\n    WHY 某些 errors 可修复而某些不可修复（scope errors 的 0% Δ），贡献于 boundary characterization 而非\n    repair improvement。\n\n    '\n- name: Statistical Significance Testing\n  plan_id: exp-009\n  description: 对所有 benchmark 做 bootstrap 95% CI + Fisher exact test\n  expected_results:\n    folio_C1_bootstrap_95CI:\n    - 0.333\n    - 0.461\n    folio_C2_bootstrap_95CI:\n    - 0.782\n    - 0.934\n    folio_C4_bootstrap_95CI_all_mode:\n    - -0.8\n    - 11.2\n    folio_C4_fisher_p_all_mode: 0.078\n    folio_C4_bootstrap_95CI_excl_unknown:\n    - -7.5\n    - 7.5\n    folio_C4_fisher_p_excl_unknown: 1.0\n    folio_C5_bootstrap_95CI:\n    - 0.735\n    - 0.939\n    proofwriter_C1_bootstrap_95CI:\n    - 0.128\n    - 0.218\n    proofwriter_C2_bootstrap_95CI:\n    - 0.472\n    - 0.771\n    proofwriter_C4_fisher_p: 0.31\n    math_C1_bootstrap_95CI:\n    - 0.093\n    - 0.194\n    math_C2_bootstrap_95CI:\n    - 0.385\n    - 0.762\n    math_C4_fisher_p: 0.82\n    benchmarks_with_C4_significant: 0\n    benchmarks_with_C1C2_significant: 1\n  result_rationale: '统计显著性结果在 worst-case 下呈现清晰的 \"FOLIO-only\" 格局： (1) FOLIO 的 C1（39.6%）和\n    C2（86.8%）CI 不跨零，统计显著。但 C4 All-mode（+5.2pp） 的 Fisher exact p=0.078，未达 0.05 阈值——这是因为\n    C4 的 base rate 比较（targeted vs blind） 在 N=96 paired samples 上 power 不足。Bootstrap\n    CI [-0.8, 11.2] 跨零。Excl-Unknown 的 C4 delta=0.0pp 显然不显著。 (2) ProofWriter 的 C2 CI\n    [0.472, 0.771] 跨 65% threshold——无法 claim \"high precision\"。 C4 p=0.31，far from\n    significant。 (3) MATH 更差：C2 CI [0.385, 0.762] 极宽（N=24 disagreement samples），C4\n    p=0.82。 (4) 没有任何 benchmark 的 C4 达到统计显著性。只有 FOLIO 的 C1 和 C2 显著。 这意味着论文能统计支撑的 claim\n    仅限于 \"FOLIO 上 disagree rate substantial 且 diagnostically precise\"，repair 和跨域泛化均无统计支撑。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - table_id: tab-exp009-1\n    caption: Statistical Significance Summary Across Benchmarks\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - FOLIO\n    - ProofWriter\n    - MATH\n    rows:\n    - - C1 Disagree Rate\n      - 39.6% [33.3, 46.1]**\n      - 17.0% [12.8, 21.8]*\n      - 14.0% [9.3, 19.4]*\n    - - C2 Precision\n      - 86.8% [78.2, 93.4]**\n      - 63.2% [47.2, 77.1]\n      - 58.3% [38.5, 76.2]\n    - - C4 Δ All-mode\n      - +5.2pp [-0.8, 11.2]\n      - +1.8pp [-4.2, 7.8]\n      - -0.5pp [-9.1, 8.1]\n    - - C4 Fisher p (All)\n      - '0.078'\n      - '0.31'\n      - '0.82'\n    - - C4 Δ Excl-Unk\n      - +0.0pp [-7.5, 7.5]\n      - -2.1pp [-9.8, 5.6]\n      - -3.2pp [-14.1, 7.7]\n    - - C5 Localization\n      - 85.4% [73.5, 93.9]**\n      - 72.0% [58.1, 83.5]*\n      - 63.0% [44.7, 79.0]\n  - table_id: tab-exp009-2\n    caption: Statistical Power Analysis\n    columns:\n    - Test\n    - N (effective)\n    - Observed Effect\n    - Power at α=0.05\n    - N needed for 80% power\n    rows:\n    - - FOLIO C4 Fisher\n      - 96 pairs\n      - +5.2pp\n      - '0.42'\n      - ~280\n    - - ProofWriter C4 Fisher\n      - ~120 pairs\n      - +1.8pp\n      - '0.12'\n      - ~2400\n    - - MATH C4 Fisher\n      - ~86 pairs\n      - -0.5pp\n      - '0.05'\n      - N/A (null effect)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Forest plot: C4 delta with 95% CI across three benchmarks, showing all CIs crossing\n    zero — no benchmark achieves statistical significance for repair'\n  - 'Forest plot: C2 precision with 95% CI, showing FOLIO clearly above 65% threshold\n    while ProofWriter and MATH CIs cross it'\n  - 'Power curve: statistical power vs sample size for C4 Fisher test at observed\n    effect sizes, showing FOLIO needs ~280 samples for 80% power'\n  analysis: '统计检验结果是 worst-case 的 \"nail in the coffin\" for the general framework narrative。\n    C4（repair）在任何 benchmark 上都不显著，C2（precision）仅在 FOLIO 上显著。 这直接支持核心假设 \"仅 FOLIO 单\n    benchmark 数据可靠\"。 在 reframed narrative 中，这驱动两个调整：(1) 诚实报告 all CIs，不 overclaim；\n    (2) 将 FOLIO 的 power analysis 作为 future work 的 guide（需要 ~280 samples 才能 confirm\n    C4 effect），承认当前 sample size 是 limitation。 注意 FOLIO C4 的 p=0.078 是 borderline——在\n    reframed 的 \"case study\" narrative 下， 可以 report 为 \"marginally significant trend\"\n    而非 hard claim，这在 EMNLP 可接受。\n\n    '\n- name: Qwen3-8B Ablation\n  plan_id: exp-010\n  description: 低能力模型上的诊断率和分歧率测试\n  expected_results:\n    C1_disagree_rate: 0.52\n    C2_diagnostic_precision: 0.61\n    C3_error_types: 3\n    C4_targeted_vs_blind_delta_pp: 1.5\n    C5_localization_accuracy: 0.68\n    fol_code_error_ratio: '4:1'\n    fol_crash_rate: 0.12\n    code_crash_rate: 0.08\n    both_wrong_rate: 0.28\n  result_rationale: 'Qwen3-8B 的 disagree rate 上升到 52%（vs 32B 的 39.6%），表面上看更多分歧。但 diagnostic\n    precision 降至 61%——更多分歧是 \"noise\" 而非 \"signal\"。原因： (1) 8B 模型在两种表征上都犯更多错误，both-wrong\n    rate 从 ~10% 飙升到 28%。大量 disagreements 来自 \"两侧都错但错误方式不同\"，这类分歧无 diagnostic value。\n    (2) FOL:Code asymmetry 减弱（4:1 vs 9:1）——8B 的 FOL 生成能力退化明显（Z3 crash rate 12%，因为生成的\n    FOL 语法更常出错），削弱了 \"FOL 作为 reliable reference\" 的前提。 (3) C4 delta 仅 1.5pp——更多错误不等于更多可修复的错误。低能力模型的\n    errors 更 fundamental （理解错误而非形式化错误），repair 更难。 (4) C5 localization 降至 68%——当 both-wrong\n    rate 高时，\"哪侧错了\" 的判定本身就更模糊。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - table_id: tab-exp010-1\n    caption: 'Model Capability Ablation: Qwen3-8B vs Qwen3-32B (FOLIO)'\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Qwen3-8B\n    - Qwen3-32B\n    - Δ\n    rows:\n    - - C1 Disagree Rate\n      - 52.0%\n      - 39.6%\n      - +12.4pp\n    - - C2 Precision\n      - 61.0%\n      - 86.8%\n      - -25.8pp\n    - - C4 Δ All-mode\n      - +1.5pp\n      - +5.2pp\n      - -3.7pp\n    - - C5 Localization\n      - 68.0%\n      - 85.4%\n      - -17.4pp\n    - - FOL:Code Error Ratio\n      - '4:1'\n      - '9:1'\n      - Asymmetry reduced\n    - - Both-Wrong Rate\n      - 28.0%\n      - ~10%\n      - +18pp\n    - - FOL Crash Rate\n      - 12.0%\n      - ~2%\n      - +10pp\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter: model capability (8B vs 32B) on x-axis, disagree rate vs diagnostic\n    precision on y-axis, showing inverse relationship — more disagreement but less\n    informative'\n  analysis: '8B 结果揭示了 cross-representation diagnosis 的另一个 applicability condition：\n    模型能力需要足够高，使得至少一种表征是 reliable 的。当模型能力不足时，both-wrong rate 上升，分歧变成噪声。这支持 \"asymmetric\n    reliability\" 作为 necessary condition 的论点。 在 reframed narrative 中，这与 MATH 的 failure\n    mode 形成呼应——无论是因为 domain （MATH 中 CoT 和 SymPy 都 fallible）还是因为 model capability（8B\n    中 FOL 也不可靠）， 一旦 asymmetric reliability 被打破，diagnosis 就失效。\n\n    '\n- name: GPQA Diamond Extension\n  plan_id: exp-011\n  description: 科学知识推理领域，CoT vs Python 验证代码\n  expected_results:\n    N_samples: 150\n    C1_disagree_rate: 0.11\n    C2_diagnostic_precision: 0.56\n    C4_delta_pp: -1.8\n    C5_localization_accuracy: 0.6\n    cot_code_error_ratio: 1.3:1\n    correlated_failure_rate: 0.38\n    code_not_applicable_rate: 0.35\n    mvp_pass_count: 0/5\n  result_rationale: 'GPQA Diamond 是 worst-case 的极端表现。disagree rate 仅 11%，precision\n    56%（接近随机）。 核心原因：科学推理（物理/化学/生物）中 Python 代码的角色与逻辑域完全不同——大部分 GPQA 问题 需要 domain knowledge\n    和 conceptual reasoning，Python 只能验证计算步骤但无法验证 conceptual correctness。35% 的问题 Code\n    表征 \"不适用\"（无法有意义地用代码验证）。 CoT:Code error ratio 几乎对称（1.3:1），完全丧失了逻辑域的 asymmetric reliability。\n    Correlated failure rate 高达 38%——模型在科学知识上的盲点在两种表征上都表现出来。 C4 为负——targeted repair\n    不如 blind，因为 \"diagnosis\" 信息在科学域几乎没有 actionability。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - table_id: tab-exp011-1\n    caption: GPQA Diamond Results (N=150, Qwen3-32B)\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - GPQA\n    - MATH\n    - FOLIO\n    rows:\n    - - C1 Disagree Rate\n      - 11.0%\n      - 14.0%\n      - 39.6%\n    - - C2 Precision\n      - 56.0%\n      - 58.3%\n      - 86.8%\n    - - C4 Δ\n      - -1.8pp\n      - -0.5pp\n      - +5.2pp\n    - - C5 Localization\n      - 60.0%\n      - 63.0%\n      - 85.4%\n    - - Error Ratio\n      - 1.3:1\n      - 1.8:1\n      - '9:1'\n    - - Correlated Failure%\n      - 38.0%\n      - 31.0%\n      - 18.2%\n    - - Code N/A Rate\n      - 35.0%\n      - 8.0%\n      - 0%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Gradient heatmap: 4 benchmarks (FOLIO → ProofWriter → MATH → GPQA) showing monotonic\n    degradation of all metrics, establishing the applicability spectrum'\n  analysis: GPQA 完成了 \"applicability spectrum\" 的构建：FOLIO（强信号）→ ProofWriter（弱信号）→ MATH（噪声）→\n    GPQA（失效）。关键维度是 representation asymmetry 和 formalization-vs-knowledge error ratio。GPQA\n    的 35% code-not-applicable rate 揭示了一个 fundamental limitation： cross-representation\n    diagnosis 要求两种表征都能 meaningfully encode the reasoning， 而科学推理中 Code 常常只能部分覆盖推理过程。\n    这在 reframed narrative 中作为 applicability conditions 的最外层边界。\n","numLines":1026,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1026}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01H1G18WarAYTcSUutWCzcas","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've now read both the PDF paper and the review context YAML. Let me understand what I need to do:\n\n1. Conduct a full review with 2 reviewers:\n   - R1: Methods + Experiments\n   - R2: Novelty + Related Work\n2. Follow the roundtable process: Step 1 (independent) → Step 2 (cross-share) → Step 3 (converge) → Step 4 (synthesize)\n\nLet me dispatch both reviewers in parallel for Step 1 (independent reviews), then proceed through the roundtable.\n\nLet me first summarize what I've read:\n\n\nThe paper investigates how disagreements between two different formalizations of reasoning problems—one in first-order logic verified by Z3, the other in executable Python—can identify formalization errors in LLM outputs. The approach shows strong performance on FOLIO with high precision and localization rates, but effectiveness drops significantly across other datasets like ProofWriter, MATH, and GPQA, suggesting the method's applicability depends on specific problem characteristics.\n\nTwo key requirements emerge: the two representations must have asymmetric reliability, and errors must stem primarily from formalization rather than reasoning itself. While the repair mechanism provides only marginal improvements and isn't statistically significant, selection-based approaches outperform repair by a meaningful margin. The error taxonomy developed offers useful descriptive insights but lacks prescriptive power for fixing problems. The experiments comprehensively cover cross-model comparisons, dataset extensions, repair mechanisms, and the relative effectiveness of selection versus repair strategies.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":32888,"cache_read_input_tokens":23110,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":32888},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3e779216-cbf6-4585-b15e-4c991e2c88e5","uuid":"9abc1450-e406-4b14-8edc-0a482a712134"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01H1G18WarAYTcSUutWCzcas","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"论文和实验设计已读完。现在启动 Step 1：两位 Reviewer 独立审稿。"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":32888,"cache_read_input_tokens":23110,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":32888},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3e779216-cbf6-4585-b15e-4c991e2c88e5","uuid":"c27bf8a1-dfac-4435-a49b-99482cc021dc"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01H1G18WarAYTcSUutWCzcas","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Pqgt8BbUnt969LntYUvNb6","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a top ML venue review. Your focus is **methods and experiments**. Review the paper below and produce a structured review. Use a 6-point scale (1=Strong Reject, 6=Strong Accept), targeting ~25% acceptance rate.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\n**Title**: \"When and Why Cross-Representation Disagreement Works: A Case Study in Formal Logic Reasoning\"\n\n**Core idea**: When an LLM formalizes an NL reasoning problem into two representations—FOL (verified by Z3) and executable Python code—disagreements between outputs serve as a diagnostic signal for formalization errors. The paper studies when/why this works and when it fails.\n\n**Method (Section 3)**:\n- Given NL problem x, prompt model M to produce FOL (checked by Z3) and Python code\n- Disagreement detected when a_FOL ≠ a_Code (C1)\n- Among disagreeing samples, measure diagnostic precision (C2), error taxonomy (C3), targeted vs blind repair delta (C4), error localization (C5)\n- Two proposed applicability conditions: (1) asymmetric reliability between representations, (2) formalization-dominated errors\n\n**Experimental Setup (Section 4)**:\n- 4 benchmarks: FOLIO (N=192), ProofWriter (N=300), MATH Level 5 (N=200), GPQA Diamond (N=150)\n- Primary model: Qwen3-32B. Ablations: Qwen3-8B, DeepSeek V4 Pro\n- 5 evaluation criteria (C1-C5), bootstrap 95% CIs, Fisher's exact test\n\n**Key Results**:\n- FOLIO: 39.6% disagree [33.3,46.1]**, 86.8% precision [78.2,93.4]**, 85.4% localization [73.5,93.9]**, 9:1 FOL:Code error ratio\n- ProofWriter: 17% disagree, 63.2% precision, 72% localization, 7:1 ratio\n- MATH: 14% disagree, 58.3% precision, 63% localization, 1.8:1 ratio, 31% correlated failures\n- GPQA: 11% disagree, 56% precision, 60% localization, 1.3:1 ratio, 38% correlated failures\n- C4 (repair): +5.2pp on FOLIO (p=0.078, CI crosses zero), no significance elsewhere\n- C4 Excl-Unknown: 0.0pp on FOLIO — entire signal from GT=Unknown samples (confound: Python can't implement 3-valued logic)\n- Selection > Repair by 4.5pp (68% vs 63.5%)\n- Multi-round repair: diminishing returns (5.2→2.6→2.1pp)\n- Error taxonomy: 1.0pp prescriptive advantage (p=0.68, n.s.)\n- Cross-model ablation: only 1.5pp reduction in correlated failures (spec-level ambiguity is root cause, not model bias)\n- Qwen3-8B: more disagree (52%) but lower precision (61%), both-wrong 28%, 4:1 ratio\n- Power analysis: FOLIO C4 needs ~280 samples for 80% power\n\n**Tables**: 16 tables covering all experiments\n**Paper length**: 12 pages (10 content + references)\n\n**Experiment coverage vs plan**: The review_context.yaml lists 10 imagined experiments (exp-002 through exp-011). ALL are covered in the paper.\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nEvaluate:\n1. **Methodological soundness**: Is the experimental design rigorous? Are the metrics well-defined? Are the controls appropriate?\n2. **Experimental thoroughness**: Are the experiments sufficient to support the claims? Are there missing experiments or ablations?\n3. **Statistical rigor**: Are the statistical methods appropriate? Are the CIs and significance tests correctly applied?\n4. **Reproducibility**: Is there enough detail to reproduce?\n5. **Clarity of experimental presentation**: Are results clearly presented?\n\n## Output Format\n\n```\n## R1: Methods and Experiments\n\n### Summary\n[2-3 sentences]\n\n### Strengths\n- S1: ...\n- S2: ...\n...\n\n### Weaknesses\n- W1: ...\n- W2: ...\n...\n\n### Questions for Authors\n- Q1: ...\n...\n\n### Minor Issues\n- ...\n\n### Scores\n- Soundness: X/5\n- Contribution: X/5  \n- Presentation: X/5\n- Overall: X/6\n- Confidence: X/5\n```\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":32888,"cache_read_input_tokens":23110,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":32888},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3e779216-cbf6-4585-b15e-4c991e2c88e5","uuid":"71d03a46-59ab-4425-bf41-14186b78086d"}
